675","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/70918557cadb78b72877efac0cf725b347aee675","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/70918557cadb78b72877efac0cf725b347aee675"}]},{"sha":"70918557cadb78b72877efac0cf725b347aee675","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKDcwOTE4NTU3Y2FkYjc4YjcyODc3ZWZhYzBjZjcyNWIzNDdhZWU2NzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Connor Braa","email":"3478454+cwlbraa@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-19T17:45:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-19T17:45:55Z"},"message":"feat(sdk-py): add decrypt replacement result (#8598)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add `DecryptResult` with plaintext and optional replacement ciphertext\n- keep raw decrypt return values backward compatible\n- export the result from `langgraph_sdk`\n\n## Merge order\n\nIndependent of langgraph-api#3884. Merge and release this SDK change\nbefore LSD-1489 consumes the result in langgraph-api.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `make format`\n- `make lint`\n- `make test`","tree":{"sha":"a56b97b527bb0a7b5e560badea4f6a91705069a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/a56b97b527bb0a7b5e560badea4f6a91705069a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/70918557cadb78b72877efac0cf725b347aee675","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhevTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7WoQAElUEt5uiVkMJMQrwO1k1otZ\n0L/HLyzIjB8dQ+X22OaDfi/Kbl1xtbUtHmWBc9F2xsojcDWw6wml9dG31+bos0bT\nsbD6IltDQSc4iLhMCY//xcZa+5lkkrfEF529KXteyxnd3kXNl75D4plFWE62lC8I\nEbNJi6WectoUB8rErLzQOhE3XyC7GLnm9VXgO/wdr4ImPuzGxgxyx3YKn1+22VpV\nu7ZjjbjJJRShgasasSred0g6g0T/Cj7wb0Y5/2TLxAbJV7W8FSQTN3nIphK3zzlx\nbi/g/Ms8ky4U6JJxH3CVqTF2nZf/GzJiqVuh6eF7GlzHtKkkdO+5AmAl/Q20lyqw\n7oO16bYTbqi+RY+2PexVqxZEt1woQnq7qP2ttR0e1HWat1plABFVbLCZT7x7cVhY\nVGDo7BrwgUnGCyrb51paKH1m00tb8rREo4sTzpHijRzpsEqVmUXJJ0RsHvV/IAhq\nXZnbl/bkCVyofC6StEjC6L1G8CSoFDSMyfYDVIetlvCYI5/jKaugcaZKn9S/HVg2\njfAzk7FN9BPVvE6Z97jenjVnTf+VxNmIuhQdGi+cuzPJ7zo+RlR3BVLpsY0OT6/o\nI06lVlHL5IBVahgrY1TIarCs0M65e06dqalA8/8O5G2DbFZAIs3YL6wxL5X/9owt\n5nJCtAaqD29EJPoF+kV4\n=i2UY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a56b97b527bb0a7b5e560badea4f6a91705069a3\nparent 1e44bda48ff4982b8ccfeec9c14156ea9e8ae5a2\nauthor Connor Braa <3478454+cwlbraa@users.noreply.github.com> 1787161555 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787161555 -0700\n\nfeat(sdk-py): add decrypt replacement result (#8598)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add `DecryptResult` with plaintext and optional replacement ciphertext\n- keep raw decrypt return values backward compatible\n- export the result from `langgraph_sdk`\n\n## Merge order\n\nIndependent of langgraph-api#3884. Merge and release this SDK change\nbefore LSD-1489 consumes the result in langgraph-api.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `make format`\n- `make lint`\n- `make test`","verified_at":"2026-08-19T17:45:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/70918557cadb78b72877efac0cf725b347aee675","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/70918557cadb78b72877efac0cf725b347aee675","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/70918557cadb78b72877efac0cf725b347aee675/comments","author":{"login":"cwlbraa","id":3478454,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0Nzg0NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3478454?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa","html_url":"https://github.com/cwlbraa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1e44bda48ff4982b8ccfeec9c14156ea9e8ae5a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/1e44bda48ff4982b8ccfeec9c14156ea9e8ae5a2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/1e44bda48ff4982b8ccfeec9c14156ea9e8ae5a2"}]},{"sha":"1e44bda48ff4982b8ccfeec9c14156ea9e8ae5a2","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKDFlNDRiZGE0OGZmNDk4MmI4Y2NmZWVjOWMxNDE1NmVhOWU4YWU1YTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Igor Soarez","email":"i@soarez.me","date":"2026-08-18T19:04:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T19:04:28Z"},"message":"fix(langgraph): detect subgraphs from bytecode instead of source (#8569)\n\nFixes langchain-ai/langgraph#8559\n\n`find_subgraph_pregel` runs once per node at build time and recovers\neach node function's reachable values with `inspect.getsource` +\n`ast.parse`; langchain-ai/langgraph#8559 measures that source parsing at\n80% of `StateGraph.compile()`. This replaces it with a `dis` walk over\n`func.__code__`, which reads the same information already in memory.\n\nClosure cells and the globals named in `co_names` supply the values\ndirectly, and a walk over the instruction stream recovers the attribute\npaths the function actually takes. The closure alone cannot express\nthose: a captured `holder` whose graph lives at `holder.graph` is\nreachable only if something records that `graph` is loaded off `holder`.\n\nBoth implementations over-declare — a node can reference a graph it\nnever invokes — and this one over-declares a different set. It no longer\nreports a graph named only along an attribute path in code the compiler\nremoved; such a path cannot execute, so that entry was always a phantom.\nNothing that can actually run stopped being detected.\n`find_subgraph_pregel` returns the first `PregelProtocol` it finds, so\nthe remaining extra candidates only widen detection.\n\n## Release note\n\nSubgraph auto-detection now reads node functions' bytecode instead of\nparsing their source. Graph builds with many function-backed nodes are\nsubstantially faster, and subgraphs are now detected inside functions\nwith no retrievable source — defined in a REPL or notebook cell, or via\n`exec` — where detection previously failed silently and returned\nnothing.\n\n## Performance\n\nAgainst\n[langgraph-build-bench](<https://github.com/soarez/langgraph-build-bench>)\n— 713 nodes, 500 state fields, 264 tools; CPython 3.12.8, Apple silicon:\n\n```\nbefore   build 1412 ms   subgraph detection 1132 ms  (80%)\nafter    build  286 ms   subgraph detection    4 ms   (2%)\n```\n\n**4.9x on total build, \\~266x on detection.** The bench prints whole ms;\nat full precision detection is 1139 ms -> 4.23 ms.\n\nCo-authored-by: Elior Nataf Lackritz <elior.nataflackritz@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"554142294c680ddefa9eb6441815f869e8638746","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/554142294c680ddefa9eb6441815f869e8638746"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/1e44bda48ff4982b8ccfeec9c14156ea9e8ae5a2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhKy9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnHoQAKzDqGen70sLd0Fffd42pu46\ntyDOputBhz3kOsE+plPDRsGIVZnc3BJYe0pq4Q7DnNw8f17+wdfPm69kd7HorBZs\nfEBqWBMKhaMN1vtt7kzXQOHQutaSIMyTIHyKex66HgouPp9NR6fLb1l2zQu3zrmm\nyulAAiigrht/dVQWIpZFvCu5Vv0wlRufMquZQg5vfRafGoV1bIn4HTUJypnGsUeY\n7XEnBS2cSt7gO3PlyhqwXdqqsJvDVn3kA+Ez9LLXK3gmRnBeW2Dk49x1E8HSQ9uL\n/OFiTgma/rnsXPJgMY0N49sNvZnd6jBLJclzh5bwCenqZOkHR+zif4SRmxLGjJPe\nsnSBr0mPBJr8Iye2fZwDVhDNCAaBDwMmSJMgRxHpJnovKUyHGjNNy/ne8w19pMWw\nd/Dd7cOb3rKphl8MsUfR/oyPh+377waQ4Xamx3PK2fXhTKvT+TomTXuhQfS/4p/H\nSqIFew9lorlpOlLUFZzYuYb7L30D3FnIoMWxJyJZXqZuzA/CtyMSF8IkhukndggI\noqti/67O4Z9ZypU+ZgPE7Nvpr2t9FQwkrM8Rhfq6KJVp/mmAQFKGI+SKLSrX1e8C\n4UUV5eh22rRBotUgsmKqePqSCkoOu9FgT7WXQr82UPYIGDgsEaF9Y1eRQsxSo06J\ncxKws7NdhVo2Ob3/vXym\n=k8Jr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 554142294c680ddefa9eb6441815f869e8638746\nparent 644815f9e5bc52ad8f7a5227a456227e9c3e639b\nauthor Igor Soarez <i@soarez.me> 1787079868 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787079868 -0700\n\nfix(langgraph): detect subgraphs from bytecode instead of source (#8569)\n\nFixes langchain-ai/langgraph#8559\n\n`find_subgraph_pregel` runs once per node at build time and recovers\neach node function's reachable values with `inspect.getsource` +\n`ast.parse`; langchain-ai/langgraph#8559 measures that source parsing at\n80% of `StateGraph.compile()`. This replaces it with a `dis` walk over\n`func.__code__`, which reads the same information already in memory.\n\nClosure cells and the globals named in `co_names` supply the values\ndirectly, and a walk over the instruction stream recovers the attribute\npaths the function actually takes. The closure alone cannot express\nthose: a captured `holder` whose graph lives at `holder.graph` is\nreachable only if something records that `graph` is loaded off `holder`.\n\nBoth implementations over-declare — a node can reference a graph it\nnever invokes — and this one over-declares a different set. It no longer\nreports a graph named only along an attribute path in code the compiler\nremoved; such a path cannot execute, so that entry was always a phantom.\nNothing that can actually run stopped being detected.\n`find_subgraph_pregel` returns the first `PregelProtocol` it finds, so\nthe remaining extra candidates only widen detection.\n\n## Release note\n\nSubgraph auto-detection now reads node functions' bytecode instead of\nparsing their source. Graph builds with many function-backed nodes are\nsubstantially faster, and subgraphs are now detected inside functions\nwith no retrievable source — defined in a REPL or notebook cell, or via\n`exec` — where detection previously failed silently and returned\nnothing.\n\n## Performance\n\nAgainst\n[langgraph-build-bench](<https://github.com/soarez/langgraph-build-bench>)\n— 713 nodes, 500 state fields, 264 tools; CPython 3.12.8, Apple silicon:\n\n```\nbefore   build 1412 ms   subgraph detection 1132 ms  (80%)\nafter    build  286 ms   subgraph detection    4 ms   (2%)\n```\n\n**4.9x on total build, \\~266x on detection.** The bench prints whole ms;\nat full precision detection is 1139 ms -> 4.23 ms.\n\nCo-authored-by: Elior Nataf Lackritz <elior.nataflackritz@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T19:04:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/1e44bda48ff4982b8ccfeec9c14156ea9e8ae5a2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/1e44bda48ff4982b8ccfeec9c14156ea9e8ae5a2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/1e44bda48ff4982b8ccfeec9c14156ea9e8ae5a2/comments","author":{"login":"soarez","id":1357510,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTc1MTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1357510?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/soarez","html_url":"https://github.com/soarez","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soarez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soarez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soarez/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soarez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soarez/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soarez/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soarez/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soarez/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soarez/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"644815f9e5bc52ad8f7a5227a456227e9c3e639b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/644815f9e5bc52ad8f7a5227a456227e9c3e639b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/644815f9e5bc52ad8f7a5227a456227e9c3e639b"}]},{"sha":"644815f9e5bc52ad8f7a5227a456227e9c3e639b","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKDY0NDgxNWY5ZTViYzUyYWQ4ZjdhNTIyN2E0NTYyMjdlOWMzZTYzOWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"ccurme","email":"chester.curme@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-11T13:55:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-11T13:55:59Z"},"message":"release(langgraph): 1.2.11 (#8595)","tree":{"sha":"224afb66deb22e06624b8cb7ccbeba14991f658b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/224afb66deb22e06624b8cb7ccbeba14991f658b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/644815f9e5bc52ad8f7a5227a456227e9c3e639b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqeynvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhyAQAJL78pLwyAyaeRexuOOIwbDB\no2D2cpIumM0ERFezRae+2YzaMbplywfNHJHgSc3jorXc6vtzfVksTvW8YXaPiHJj\nhGMUK+JaQtyVixxOa+pcy+rSbjOZIh15v5xGVaCzydjXFILhtdCyRFbKsp4w+nhV\njTs73i9R9lUwZTLH0WO+JBA3drRLe2sGm+1htmByQKRAw/gTGn8SS7UZnDa//qgy\nkXMmP3t8TFqosj/HCMB/LDiuN80Bghz73oGou4Mxa9xsEjkAg54VuEVNqwCQn0c1\nJ+/P6QUopDb4JBLzz83R0e7cd4ssZlC2HSo8496zxqc1wibHDPIYUiH5ipXgfsHs\n0BWsvpfMtmFYmXNzvW5fSxbxSp0rhNHL8vpicgqsbVtkXD9Ni/Uokn8BH+6C9auk\nloIO0Rd5X2fhNkZTau9nJuCMP4/82ek/ZI/IUDPdlEPzSpN+FrpqTcPBqikrKvEj\nhb+aOSwEi7P7YoXS+Xhh8WpNs5HURVbm3K6eDwPKFQNn50h0+DyVAiBV4VzFyXzB\naqDw/x/4hBjDk/Fbuz6F6NpJFQe03/zvCn2O+ggDxWjCanY5UDPIZx6AyYVIgJh3\nOV8DIIII9fUgAdZ0ljwvSrHUhtcsd9Qw4to7PTMOWBolQM/gq0KDO6ffy1fsdqJB\n9DnmD4XYOrZEu15PsJ2n\n=w1f6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 224afb66deb22e06624b8cb7ccbeba14991f658b\nparent 7d6b5790ba84ce38c26f27a533d8419a31103c36\nauthor ccurme <chester.curme@gmail.com> 1786456559 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786456559 -0400\n\nrelease(langgraph): 1.2.11 (#8595)","verified_at":"2026-08-11T13:56:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/644815f9e5bc52ad8f7a5227a456227