t rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-25T08:00:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/30c4d58db86455128e42ddec96b1ba53c553ba22","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/30c4d58db86455128e42ddec96b1ba53c553ba22","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/30c4d58db86455128e42ddec96b1ba53c553ba22/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1f2f88b2b74aa4e26c6a8be877dcb95bad2cef48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/1f2f88b2b74aa4e26c6a8be877dcb95bad2cef48","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/1f2f88b2b74aa4e26c6a8be877dcb95bad2cef48"}]},{"sha":"1f2f88b2b74aa4e26c6a8be877dcb95bad2cef48","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKDFmMmY4OGIyYjc0YWE0ZTI2YzZhOGJlODc3ZGNiOTViYWQyY2VmNDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-25T08:00:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-25T08:00:25Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump js-yaml from 4.2.0 to 4.3.0 in /libs/cli/js-monorepo-example (#8438)\n\nBumps [js-yaml](https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml) from 4.2.0 to 4.3.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md\">js-yaml's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>4.3.0, 3.15.0 - 2026-06-27</h2>\n<h3>Security</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Backported <code>maxTotalMergeKeys</code> option.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[5.2.0] - 2026-06-26</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Added <code>maxTotalMergeKeys</code> (10000) loader option to limit\nthe total number of\nkeys processed by YAML merge (<code>&lt;&lt;</code>) across one\n<code>load()</code> / <code>loadAll()</code> call.</li>\n<li>Added <code>maxAliases</code> (-1) loader option to limit the number\nof YAML aliases per\ndocument.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Removed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>maxMergeSeqLength</code> replaced with\n<code>maxTotalMergeKeys</code> for limiting YAML merge\nprocessing.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Fixed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Round-trip of integers with exponential form (&gt;=\n<code>1e21</code>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[5.1.0] - 2026-06-23</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Collection tags can finalize an incrementally populated carrier into\na\ndifferent result value.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Changed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[breaking] <code>quoteStyle</code> now selects the preferred quote\nstyle; use the\nrestored <code>forceQuotes</code> option to force quoting non-key\nstrings.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[5.0.0] - 2026-06-20</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Added named exports for schemas, tags, parser events and AST\nutilities.</li>\n<li>Reworked <code>JSON_SCHEMA</code> and <code>CORE_SCHEMA</code> with\nspec-compliant scalar resolution\nrules, and added <code>YAML11_SCHEMA</code>.</li>\n<li>Added <code>realMapTag</code> for lossless mappings with non-string\nand complex keys.\nObject-based mappings now reject complex keys instead of stringifying\nthem.</li>\n<li>Added <code>dump()</code> <code>transform</code> option for changing\nthe generated AST before\nrendering.</li>\n<li>Added <code>dump()</code> options <code>seqInlineFirst</code>,\n<code>flowBracketPadding</code>,\n<code>flowSkipCommaSpace</code>, <code>flowSkipColonSpace</code>,\n<code>quoteFlowKeys</code>, <code>quoteStyle</code> and\n<code>tagBeforeAnchor</code>.</li>\n<li>Added formal data layers (events and AST) for modular data\npipelines.\n<ul>\n<li>Added low-level parser (to events), presenter and visitor APIs.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Added the <a href=\"https://github.com/yaml/yaml-test-suite\">YAML\nTest Suite</a> to the\ntest set.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Changed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>See the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/blob/master/docs/migrate_v4_to_v5.md\">migration\nguide</a> for upgrade notes.</li>\n<li>Rewritten in TypeScript and reorganized the public API around flat\nnamed\nexports.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/33d05b5d29a8c21360f620f7e1c1706e24522eda\"><code>33d05b5</code></a>\n4.3.0 released</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/663bfab6db2b4a146a9366fd685f069345be4ddb\"><code>663bfab</code></a>\nDrop demo publish, to not override new v5 one.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/1cb8c7b94bf75e15116869c1c0482dcb22785986\"><code>1cb8c7b</code></a>\nAdd v4-legacy tag for publish</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/02f27afad532763263cd2b6be35c24ee8e1f6157\"><code>02f27af</code></a>\nRestore umd builds back to es5</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/8be84edaf15e7c394fa3b813179d1bcc280e87fb\"><code>8be84ed</code></a>\nFix es5 compatibility</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/59423c6f8cdc78742ac00e25a4dd39ef16b702e4\"><code>59423c6</code></a>\nReplace <code>maxMergeSeqLength</code> option with\n<code>maxTotalMergeKeys</code> (more robust). Ba...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/6842ef6a02df01ca7282ea01dc3c70787710c05d\"><code>6842ef6</code></a>\ndoc polish</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/compare/4.2.0...4.3.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=js-yaml&package-manager=npm_and_yarn&previous-version=4.2.0&new-version=4.3.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e10cfe44580efdda8935552bcc7bdeceac6b29e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/e10cfe44580efdda8935552bcc7bdeceac6b29e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/1f2f88b2b74aa4e26c6a8be877dcb95bad2cef48","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZG0ZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvsUQAEgjl2qGyg2ADCnz4h0cVPg1\nq8AMixNTq/xFWohsGWvtZ7bL+WuR21NcCW21sUAOiUj/n+P7RrGbLYRtmInSxHyL\n3tvmx51C+uQ3iAPOfqtJTpcIe2N/G2dOFuYT5JjI2MDd/Q9FmVW61y4H6uQQ+9SM\n8Ly+Nh4753Lb1Xe3MBNKtwHU2qzezCP532vAbiE5dxtE7fUwNFH2Tocz6sSTrzk+\nUvqU/8M5pRP4mru1guWgAZ655VGFRmCnvWjPUI/kdsldWGVs9XsdRLp+eZEq32LI\nTDlFRM0C8tUU6VYkmP0cUqM77e28fMPpsA1R10dHM9yo5T1elzgdR9RmX0GAzBL5\nxSaSu4oSiULF7iUm9r3487eLsD30AzX5ERDB1MmjzccAfj3xWRyHit/A2YNPg0I9\ng6CRLv4cnZ1kNYpSOnkVYhHVZ/kFTqhUl8g2ELySEsBXSSUceeJ6SFYunnl/Hcb/\nWzbI8s4DlTSogdtHKDXnduP+sA9qLdDNe5vdJMLz4np5cK7ofC/uuTN0PUCGsMcw\nEelWeIRZz6hvo0l1H9X0MidadKzgSUjvnbZXMqoBrKC2mA4CRct+98ctWmO6yuZH\nc/lcM/QICztJmKgTS887gZ/FX+IhACUJiY40MwVbuG5igrkQEYOiw6dmWFxx0sNg\nOLEaXmZalVn3UdCqE10k\n=nPaX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e10cfe44580efdda8935552bcc7bdeceac6b29e6\nparent 270820363d56cf8a8e594d2d3b19d543230337fb\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784966425 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784966425 -0700\n\nchore(deps): bump js-yaml from 4.2.0 to 4.3.0 in /libs/cli/js-monorepo-example (#8438)\n\nBumps [js-yaml](https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml) from 4.2.0 to 4.3.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md\">js-yaml's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>4.3.0, 3.15.0 - 2026-06-27</h2>\n<h3>Security</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Backported <code>maxTotalMergeKeys</code> option.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[5.2.0] - 2026-06-26</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Added <code>maxTotalMergeKeys</code> (10000) loader option to limit\nthe total number of\nkeys processed by YAML merge (<code>&lt;&lt;</code>) across one\n<code>load()</code> / <code>loadAll()</code> call.</li>\n<li>Added <code>maxAliases</code> (-1) loader option to limit the number\nof YAML aliases per\ndocument.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Removed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>maxMergeSeqLength</code> replaced with\n<code>maxTotalMergeKeys</code> for limiting YAML merge\nprocessing.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Fixed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Round-trip of integers with exponential form (&gt;=\n<code>1e21</code>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[5.1.0] - 2026-06-23</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Collection tags can finalize an incrementally populated carrier into\na\ndifferent result value.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Changed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[breaking] <code>quoteStyle</code> now selects the preferred quote\nstyle; use the\nrestored <code>forceQuotes</code> option to force quoting non-key\nstrings.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[5.0.0] - 2026-06-20</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Added named exports for schemas, tags, parser events and AST\nutilities.</li>\n<li>Reworked <code>JSON_SCHEMA</code> and <code>CORE_SCHEMA</code> with\nspec-compliant scalar resolution\nrules, and added <code>YAML11_SCHEMA</code>.</li>\n<li>Added <code>realMapTag</code> for lossless mappings with non-string\nand complex keys.\nObject-based mappings now reject complex keys instead of stringifying\nthem.</li>\n<li>Added <code>dump()</code> <code>transform</code> option for changing\nthe generated AST before\nrendering.</li>\n<li>Added <code>dump()</code> options <code>seqInlineFirst</code>,\n<code>flowBracketPadding</code>,\n<code>flowSkipCommaSpace</code>, <code>flowSkipColonSpace</code>,\n<code>quoteFlowKeys</code>, <code>quoteStyle</code> and\n<code>tagBeforeAnchor</code>.</li>\n<li>Added formal data layers (events and AST) for modular data\npipelines.\n<ul>\n<li>Added low-level parser (to events), presenter and visitor APIs.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Added the <a href=\"https://github.com/yaml/yaml-test-suite\">YAML\nTest Suite</a> to the\ntest set.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Changed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>See the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/blob/master/docs/migrate_v4_to_v5.md\">migration\nguide</a> for upgrade notes.</li>\n<li>Rewritten in TypeScript and reorganized the public API around flat\nnamed\nexports.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/33d05b5d29a8c21360f620f7e1c1706e24522eda\"><code>33d05b5</code></a>\n4.3.0 released</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/663bfab6db2b4a146a9366fd685f069345be4ddb\"><code>663bfab</code></a>\nDrop demo publish, to not override new v5 one.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/1cb8c7b94bf75e15116869c1c0482dcb22785986\"><code>1cb8c7b</code></a>\nAdd v4-legacy tag for publish</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/02f27afad532763263cd2b6be35c24ee8e1f6157\"><code>02f27af</code></a>\nRestore umd builds back to es5</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/8be84edaf15e7c394fa3b813179d1bcc280e87fb\"><code>8be84ed</code></a>\nFix es5 compatibility</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/59423c6f8cdc78742ac00e25a4dd39ef16b702e4\"><code>59423c6</code></a>\nReplace <code>maxMergeSeqLength</code> option with\n<code>maxTotalMergeKeys</code> (more robust). Ba...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/6842ef6a02df01ca7282ea01dc3c70787710c05d\"><code>6842ef6</code></a>\ndoc polish</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/compare/4.2.0...4.3.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=js-yaml&package-manager=npm_and_yarn&previous-version=4.2.0&new-version=4.3.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-25T08:00:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/1f2f88b2b74aa4e26c6a8be877dcb95bad2cef48","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/1f2f88b2b74aa4e26c6a8be877dcb95bad2cef48","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/1f2f88b2b74aa4e26c6a8be877dcb95bad2cef48/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"270820363d56cf8a8e594d2d3b19d543230337fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/270820363d56cf8a8e594d2d3b19d543230337fb","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/270820363d56cf8a8e594d2d3b19d543230337fb"}]},{"sha":"270820363d56cf8a8e594d2d3b19d543230337fb","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKDI3MDgyMDM2M2Q1NmNmOGE4ZTU5NGQyZDNiMTlkNTQzMjMwMzM3ZmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-25T07:34:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-25T07:34:37Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump setuptools from 82.0.1 to 83.0.0 in /libs/cli (#8434)\n\nBumps [setuptools](https://github.com/pypa/setuptools) from 82.0.1 to\n83.0.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/blob/main/NEWS.rst\">setuptools's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>v83.0.0</h1>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Require Python 3.10 or later.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Bugfixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>MANIFEST.in</code> matching (via <code>FileList</code>) is now\ninsensitive to Unicode\nnormalization form. A pattern authored in one form (e.g. NFC, as\ntypically\nsaved by editors) now matches a file whose name is stored on disk in\nanother\n(e.g. NFD, as produced by macOS APFS/HFS+). Previously an\n<code>exclude</code>,\n<code>global-exclude</code>, <code>recursive-exclude</code>, or\n<code>prune</code> rule could silently\nfail to drop a non-ASCII-named file from the source distribution,\npublishing\nit despite the exclusion -- see GHSA-h35f-9h28-mq5c.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Deprecations and Removals</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>pypa/distutils#334</code></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/6519f728c6f23c992df81a5691ef7655184a20eb\"><code>6519f72</code></a>\nBump version: 82.0.1 → 83.0.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/d1151b125b29a6ee1c7db860f7ee6c365d525b5f\"><code>d1151b1</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5250\">#5250</a>\nfrom pypa/feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2df31e6a741b0fe775969618fe6a3a3d032e900\"><code>a2df31e</code></a>\nCapture removal of dry_run parameter in changelog.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/00144dc3fb6d023fd81cdc26c380a012b084df9b\"><code>00144dc</code></a>\nMoved newsfragment to the release where it occurred.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a4a5a2b160357be77626aa077ddd1d8ee53be50f\"><code>a4a5a2b</code></a>\nAdd news fragment.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/77470c23c35031c9e37d7512694ac5ca52bfcaac\"><code>77470c2</code></a>\nMerge <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/distutils\">https://github.com/pypa/distutils</a>\ninto feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/3c43897420f25a1be1afe6eaa905d056009cc736\"><code>3c43897</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5247\">#5247</a>\nfrom pypa/copilot/fix-pypy-version-issue</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/bb6ea66b4bd01cb35d7c68a1bc61b96d59190269\"><code>bb6ea66</code></a>\nBump PyPy from 3.10 to 3.11 in CI workflow</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2bc3aca2f55eb9b93ea633e58ba68170ce14451\"><code>a2bc3ac</code></a>\nFix broken intersphinx reference to build's installation docs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/2d6a739c64cfedc65e1f635af7b52340aac8d99b\"><code>2d6a739</code></a>\nUse stacked parametrize decorators instead of itertools.product</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/compare/v82.0.1...v83.0.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=setuptools&package-manager=uv&previous-version=82.0.1&new-version=83.0.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"31b65f08bc0d058e850e8e486b87d1929f466b43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/31b65f08bc0d058e850e8e486b87d1929f466b43"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/270820363d56cf8a8e594d2d3b19d543230337fb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZGcNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjBIQACO63e2gzMKb8es5q57rhG+/\nONt7Q18O4a/wvnnkiIKjhGPd6V1sXSSyiDUa8u0P6cf/vmOvQbuw+LATRG1THLpX\n4hx5zxuupZ949IaM9bh7YLKyHXfTL6sDRr4DZo3+PtNf04LVc7fLeNEnJjQ7GH8O\n4COgXkYAnznqo12xSFPozglTF9VrJmKA5kQEFY7rCwLL9BmAXBXBBpUfGFYqGDvN\nBIXDJD3oxSDZahCpA46uzYW9BHL/PL06xuARjFu/FqClQhstRMLsnS0VWJ3uUmLu\nIgTSX910fZ6R0oQTzw2hnCD4ulPXI9npzymbYU4SdX7OJucsLmmDIjKr4xZJ1qn9\n8hjYXitJq+icmk63MNR+wsACpoUDPIatm90TzRIUwcBPB4VGmkgeS7ZqkeQAhJmT\n5oiWHwXnZNLN0oYDswo5bsAI1pd4wKqt7zQgUEstMsKDnVIwXk2iYxv3tul5i5IB\nj6SMNC/wtgo8VuznJQr9aJ1fBKWmbskJOpqri6VvOHKu30MK+PQcm+XymThrHObL\nKY4GsrLmmWUCAFYlUJZrCX0EyqTjIts/dMUsUfQnKnyoMZyw0kM7cs7CK6HIFDW0\n3qzETIChAJWrQ37FxLLhZlcv1AVppAoVQMCxiEVUrW/MTYgTyMvB419uGvV2OQYV\nnoTHXrrCKAo08z2FdxDN\n=jSNW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 31b65f08bc0d058e850e8e486b87d1929f466b43\nparent 9f1e40bfeea28dee2155b4a57f5babd0a53534cf\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784964877 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784964877 -0700\n\nchore(deps): bump setuptools from 82.0.1 to 83.0.0 in /libs/cli (#8434)\n\nBumps [setuptools](https://github.com/pypa/setuptools) from 82.0.1 to\n83.0.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/blob/main/NEWS.rst\">setuptools's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>v83.0.0</h1>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Require Python 3.10 or later.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Bugfixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>MANIFEST.in</code> matching (via <code>FileList</code>) is now\ninsensitive to Unicode\nnormalization form. A pattern authored in one form (e.g. NFC, as\ntypically\nsaved by editors) now matches a file whose name is stored on disk in\nanother\n(e.g. NFD, as produced by macOS APFS/HFS+). Previously an\n<code>exclude</code>,\n<code>global-exclude</code>, <code>recursive-exclude</code>, or\n<code>prune</code> rule could silently\nfail to drop a non-ASCII-named file from the source distribution,\npublishing\nit despite the exclusion -- see GHSA-h35f-9h28-mq5c.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Deprecations and Removals</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>pypa/distutils#334</code></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/6519f728c6f23c992df81a5691ef7655184a20eb\"><code>6519f72</code></a>\nBump version: 82.0.1 → 83.0.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/d1151b125b29a6ee1c7db860f7ee6c365d525b5f\"><code>d1151b1</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5250\">#5250</a>\nfrom pypa/feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2df31e6a741b0fe775969618fe6a3a3d032e900\"><code>a2df31e</code></a>\nCapture removal of dry_run parameter in changelog.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/00144dc3fb6d023fd81cdc26c380a012b084df9b\"><code>00144dc</code></a>\nMoved newsfragment to the release where it occurred.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a4a5a2b160357be77626aa077ddd1d8ee53be50f\"><code>a4a5a2b</code></a>\nAdd news fragment.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/77470c23c35031c9e37d7512694ac5ca52bfcaac\"><code>77470c2</code></a>\nMerge <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/distutils\">https://github.com/pypa/distutils</a>\ninto feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/3c43897420f25a1be1afe6eaa905d056009cc736\"><code>3c43897</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5247\">#5247</a>\nfrom pypa/copilot/fix-pypy-version-issue</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/bb6ea66b4bd01cb35d7c68a1bc61b96d59190269\"><code>bb6ea66</code></a>\nBump PyPy from 3.10 to 3.11 in CI workflow</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2bc3aca2f55eb9b93ea633e58ba68170ce14451\"><code>a2bc3ac</code></a>\nFix broken intersphinx reference to build's installation docs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/2d6a739c64cfedc65e1f635af7b52340aac8d99b\"><code>2d6a739</code></a>\nUse stacked parametrize decorators instead of itertools.product</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/compare/v82.0.1...v83.0.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=setuptools&package-manager=uv&previous-version=82.0.1&new-version=83.0.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n