rl":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9578140336b01a748d16ea154ae6278e155983f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/9578140336b01a748d16ea154ae6278e155983f3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/9578140336b01a748d16ea154ae6278e155983f3"}]},{"sha":"9578140336b01a748d16ea154ae6278e155983f3","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKDk1NzgxNDAzMzZiMDFhNzQ4ZDE2ZWExNTRhZTYyNzhlMTU1OTgzZjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Saad Farooq","email":"saad@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-20T20:57:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-20T20:57:23Z"},"message":"feat(checkpoint,checkpoint-postgres): add opt-in omit_expired to skip expired rows on read (#8354)\n\nThe Postgres store removes expired items only via the background TTL\nsweeper, so between sweeps a read can still return a logically expired\nrow. Adds an opt-in flag so reads can filter expired rows at query time,\nclosing the window without depending on sweep cadence.\n\n## Changes\n- Add `omit_expired: bool` to `TTLConfig` (default `False`). When unset\nor `False`, behavior is unchanged\n- When enabled, inject `(expires_at IS NULL OR expires_at > NOW())` into\nthe read query builders on `BasePostgresStore`, so\n`get`/`search`/`list_namespaces` do not surface an expired row:\n- **GET** (`_get_batch_GET_ops_queries`): predicate on both the final\nSELECT *and* the refresh `UPDATE` — the update is driven from an\nunfiltered key list, so gating only the SELECT would hide an expired row\nyet still refresh it back to life.\n- **SEARCH** (`_prepare_batch_search_queries`): inside the inner scans\n(before `LIMIT`/`OFFSET`), which also gates the refresh `UPDATE` fed by\n`search_results` and keeps pagination correct\n- **list_namespaces** (`_get_batch_list_namespaces_queries`): predicate\nappended to the existing scan conditions.\n\n## Testing\n- Four behaviors covered sync + async, across the\n`default`/`pipe`/`pool` fixtures: expired-unswept row omitted from all\nread paths (with a raw SQL check proving the row is still physically\npresent), default/explicit-`False` still returns it, `refresh_ttl=True`\ndoesn't resurrect an expired row while still extending live ones, and\nsearch pagination stays correct when an expired row falls inside the\npage window.\n- Full `checkpoint-postgres` suite green on PG16 (210 passed); `ruff\nformat`/`check` clean on both packages.","tree":{"sha":"906388eb80afe7b3d27c703f4b0758216be5366d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/906388eb80afe7b3d27c703f4b0758216be5366d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/9578140336b01a748d16ea154ae6278e155983f3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXouzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAG34QAAZHpyl+Y/CQfIHi6WAkODv+\nSnlir4lFt3LgJbK+1I9ndyiT1ScYCE6YBdWLsxEkBD82qqBa1V/j9fFpMJyiQGG3\nYJ0M7DM9syqh4qNnMY5vpvXifQQG73LJfHQ5zTF8rHohIt2AG2DRLG18or90OAn+\nWQIrSsqwap9m1QbqPm88+VkjmaApNbBVO3re+JcXHveoAhiVWHxUjS2wm5GquCYt\ntwxFZocNFat3eYgeIX9eRU1RqU7DdQfV2oIY4HD4FiDlStVbvFH98GOKcqqS7Mhq\n11feYLcKCkosreTJ1fdWPEZS77E6Ow7T2caToiUlMpLKCr9q2+/eLNWFa32adjAY\ndd2wZRharQ9SbbTs3eRJG2fVIPelSJF6MCYRRarlxbjXznVw8wSXmM7fy//ZByGu\nrRrzl2OL/nNy0lH5YVQhwjK+E4zcaWZDUzV2RxaTzAnMm2IYRxC9jH/z27xdeCzF\ntC+F/HKlqUk61pvu/b5XqAwRdLSo5BzoAiZSdhLz7Fq9S9/YvcS2wTn4xOdpmdCW\nLxBwtkp2PLc7DH8AtJwzYIY53vK3PH7HUVsYFB6Z2T/4orYqnSKesrBQRTqWT+l2\niWlm4resW1JJP9aDScBTfuqI/9IjnntgIfCWsgYs7+Lsz66nOupuBnI26S683ieA\nrm2e+0AnjMytuU0P2bVW\n=PA6l\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 906388eb80afe7b3d27c703f4b0758216be5366d\nparent 49ae27c2ae983cfb92091b0dea9f7bc37a716479\nauthor Saad Farooq <saad@langchain.dev> 1784581043 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784581043 -0400\n\nfeat(checkpoint,checkpoint-postgres): add opt-in omit_expired to skip expired rows on read (#8354)\n\nThe Postgres store removes expired items only via the background TTL\nsweeper, so between sweeps a read can still return a logically expired\nrow. Adds an opt-in flag so reads can filter expired rows at query time,\nclosing the window without depending on sweep cadence.\n\n## Changes\n- Add `omit_expired: bool` to `TTLConfig` (default `False`). When unset\nor `False`, behavior is unchanged\n- When enabled, inject `(expires_at IS NULL OR expires_at > NOW())` into\nthe read query builders on `BasePostgresStore`, so\n`get`/`search`/`list_namespaces` do not surface an expired row:\n- **GET** (`_get_batch_GET_ops_queries`): predicate on both the final\nSELECT *and* the refresh `UPDATE` — the update is driven from an\nunfiltered key list, so gating only the SELECT would hide an expired row\nyet still refresh it back to life.\n- **SEARCH** (`_prepare_batch_search_queries`): inside the inner scans\n(before `LIMIT`/`OFFSET`), which also gates the refresh `UPDATE` fed by\n`search_results` and keeps pagination correct\n- **list_namespaces** (`_get_batch_list_namespaces_queries`): predicate\nappended to the existing scan conditions.\n\n## Testing\n- Four behaviors covered sync + async, across the\n`default`/`pipe`/`pool` fixtures: expired-unswept row omitted from all\nread paths (with a raw SQL check proving the row is still physically\npresent), default/explicit-`False` still returns it, `refresh_ttl=True`\ndoesn't resurrect an expired row while still extending live ones, and\nsearch pagination stays correct when an expired row falls inside the\npage window.\n- Full `checkpoint-postgres` suite green on PG16 (210 passed); `ruff\nformat`/`check` clean on both packages.","verified_at":"2026-07-20T20:57:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/9578140336b01a748d16ea154ae6278e155983f3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/9578140336b01a748d16ea154ae6278e155983f3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/9578140336b01a748d16ea154ae6278e155983f3/comments","author":{"login":"saad-supports-langchain","id":223317947,"node_id":"U_kgDODU-Puw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223317947?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saad-supports-langchain","html_url":"https://github.com/saad-supports-langchain","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saad-supports-langchain/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saad-supports-langchain/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saad-supports-langchain/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saad-supports-langchain/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saad-supports-langchain/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saad-supports-langchain/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saad-supports-langchain/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saad-supports-langchain/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saad-supports-langchain/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"49ae27c2ae983cfb92091b0dea9f7bc37a716479","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/49ae27c2ae983cfb92091b0dea9f7bc37a716479","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/49ae27c2ae983cfb92091b0dea9f7bc37a716479"}]},{"sha":"49ae27c2ae983cfb92091b0dea9f7bc37a716479","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKDQ5YWUyN2MyYWU5ODNjZmI5MjA5MWIwZGVhOWY3YmMzN2E3MTY0Nzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-15T07:55:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-15T07:55:09Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump websockets from 15.0.1 to 16.0 in /libs/sdk-py in the major group (#8253)\n\nBumps the major group in /libs/sdk-py with 1 update:\n[websockets](https://github.com/python-websockets/websockets).\n\nUpdates `websockets` from 15.0.1 to 16.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-websockets/websockets/releases\">websockets's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>16.0</h2>\n<p>See <a\nhref=\"https://websockets.readthedocs.io/en/stable/project/changelog.html\">https://websockets.readthedocs.io/en/stable/project/changelog.html</a>\nfor details.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-websockets/websockets/commit/d4303a5d3e373fc8c34177c3dec1a9c75c8865fa\"><code>d4303a5</code></a>\nRelease version 16.0.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-websockets/websockets/commit/851bcd756bf114e41438f04d928aa85838724fe1\"><code>851bcd7</code></a>\nBump pypa/cibuildwheel from 3.3.0 to 3.3.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-websockets/websockets/commit/740c8d373e10ced940fb33c3e0457991841c10c4\"><code>740c8d3</code></a>\nTemporarily remove the trio implementation.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-websockets/websockets/commit/92ea0553587ba07a4668c30dfd9e6210d9f26bc9\"><code>92ea055</code></a>\nAdd missing changelog entry.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-websockets/websockets/commit/ba74244154df5a74f044d0f8cd971acac636bb74\"><code>ba74244</code></a>\nDocument bug fix.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-websockets/websockets/commit/9410483c016463a6cd08b2a5321337b85e094f10\"><code>9410483</code></a>\nPin sphinx to avoid error in sphinxcontrib-trio.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-websockets/websockets/commit/8e4d408e17b0bfa1a91aa62e054b8786a8132231\"><code>8e4d408</code></a>\nDocument asyncio's TLS read buffer.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-websockets/websockets/commit/cb3500b0b030715dc3caa1e3ce95affe4a79b8bd\"><code>cb3500b</code></a>\nStop referring to the asyncio implementation as new.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-websockets/websockets/commit/6563a9c884d92df4c889bb174dc84a56a7377686\"><code>6563a9c</code></a>\nThe threading implementation supports max_queue.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-websockets/websockets/commit/9f17e92dbee2b9a14e02b2792cfbb127efbd4098\"><code>9f17e92</code></a>\nClarify that protocol_mutex protects pending_pings.</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-websockets/websockets/compare/15.0.1...16.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=websockets&package-manager=uv&previous-version=15.0.1&new-version=16.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> major version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's major version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's major version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> minor version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's minor version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's minor version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name>` will close this group update PR\nand stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency\n(unless you unignore this specific dependency or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name>` will remove all of the ignore\nconditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name> <ignore condition>` will\nremove the ignore condition of the specified dependency and ignore\nconditions\n\n\n</details>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: John Kennedy <65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ddcbb546b84d307bfc3be23c4c518a48d779cf09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/ddcbb546b84d307bfc3be23c4c518a48d779cf09"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/49ae27c2ae983cfb92091b0dea9f7bc37a716479","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVzzdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0uUQAK8KpwSr3ozTKEFjKPVXCpZm\nyMcEWJ4YOBBfqP21ygszzT35DLHLUWf5izy3hVPRRtlbODInQ6jQXOEc6Bd442IJ\nYC0Ocic4FiW3cYf/KgukgLdEbGu7cMacxxqgpA3Koh3UCMKwAKb7jnm5dCMmC55/\nuG6vLhKrWhyMA5frDqs15s0iM59BhbfpNmlGEM8xXuhGy40OIL9Urputp6WZubSR\nEoEU8iYQlDklpEGkz/OUYxOnOAqR6/3+g+3Qwz62HQQzzEJ2EGMWyFw2fC1S3Pj1\ncb3s/fMdo0Ul5bR/iloMr1naICmMhFgRHwokuh78tJZwxX1cJELWGfDKiMzwm21z\noZ+2/DThPvfGbgHSwzujacy8zo7qJu7rkpT8FuE