long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-19T09:56:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/e308ae99dab14bb5482c6d95b29f973a802b9f98","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/e308ae99dab14bb5482c6d95b29f973a802b9f98","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/e308ae99dab14bb5482c6d95b29f973a802b9f98/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c6eb0a20589d80e9b1964318c370a82f72889245","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/c6eb0a20589d80e9b1964318c370a82f72889245","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/c6eb0a20589d80e9b1964318c370a82f72889245"}]},{"sha":"c6eb0a20589d80e9b1964318c370a82f72889245","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKGM2ZWIwYTIwNTg5ZDgwZTliMTk2NDMxOGMzNzBhODJmNzI4ODkyNDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-19T09:56:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T09:56:06Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump js-yaml from 4.1.1 to 4.2.0 in /libs/cli/js-monorepo-example (#8143)\n\nBumps [js-yaml](https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml) from 4.1.1 to 4.2.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md\">js-yaml's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>[4.2.0] - 2026-06-01</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Added <code>docs/safety.md</code> with notes about processing\nuntrusted YAML.</li>\n<li>Added <code>maxDepth</code> (100) loader option. Not a problem, but\ngives a better\nexception instead of RangeError on stack overflow.</li>\n<li>Added <code>maxMergeSeqLength</code> (20) loader option. Not a\nproblem after <code>merge</code> fix,\nbut an additional restriction for safety.</li>\n<li>Added sourcemaps to <code>dist/</code> builds.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Changed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Stop resolving numbers with underscores as numeric scalars, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/issues/627\">#627</a>.</li>\n<li>Switched dev toolchains to Vite / neostandard.</li>\n<li>Updated demo.</li>\n<li>Reorganized tests.</li>\n<li><code>dist/</code> files are no longer kept in the repository.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Fixed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix parsing of properties on the first implicit block mapping key,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/issues/62\">#62</a>.</li>\n<li>Fix trailing whitespace handling when folding flow scalar lines, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/issues/307\">#307</a>.</li>\n<li>Reject top-level block scalars without content indentation, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/issues/280\">#280</a>.</li>\n<li>Ensure numbers survive round-trip, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/issues/737\">#737</a>.</li>\n<li>Fix test coverage for issue <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/issues/221\">#221</a>.</li>\n<li>Fix flow scalar trailing whitespace folding, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/issues/307\">#307</a>.</li>\n<li>Fix digits in YAML named tag handles.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Security</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix potential DoS via quadratic complexity in merge - deduplicate\nrepeated\nelements (makes sense for malformed files &gt; 10K).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[3.14.2] - 2025-11-15</h2>\n<h3>Security</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Backported v4.1.1 fix to v3</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commits\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=js-yaml&package-manager=npm_and_yarn&previous-version=4.1.1&new-version=4.2.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"cde2e43a5035290940ad4ccba4296f2b4cb0ca59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/cde2e43a5035290940ad4ccba4296f2b4cb0ca59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/c6eb0a20589d80e9b1964318c370a82f72889245","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNRI2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHXcQAKx4Agb9zQyHjFjZRbcBGIlb\nj4bz7+Q/+nD+cSySyMMsq5dsGMWmL48yWJw7rzeQEKtuqfIlzgR7JvYwd8CEoIgC\nYAaYYUW3TniOddLc1PCyyBFrc7tIalwMOyf+HL+Ag3vCkv7m2DqxYCp761+pCoAp\n8N9MHD7A/111OngqQTJ7a+2ko6/9R27rmxbL9yRfCif3/vAs2JREq2HhJ3rB5ZoC\n9AlIDZAZxkildht2IvcE54jqIzJ8UYdMqF2vQuHTXysmY2ZT7zc7gnyhpAtApNVB\nAdUTPyeCIe91l8U/qKaPjTdRa4B62QJP9xeMxAXF/O8u7iq49GWB09Ic9DeXTjnr\n1x+Q/IpGrg9lk5wiEgVuSlnkbSlLxDLJObkG5O7jBBoL22EeUnaonQtKqeNcQZcV\nxJB9To4mXZicZvH6eMWBqQ1DbiMHTQmYqQ/fExoA2QY1VHzW3qPqKRH2rVwsCA7q\npNqFEL+8mTucPyqhvTTZlf40kdQ2yesclyg5XDN29ALiuohlOhPIxODW7HzE0eni\n7d7mrwFylEtaO7JxLHl3tk00DxvI5DhEHPJ7FYdHuHgO4iPsX3MqCkGRJeAA1kzn\nmEdRXsykQKh1v86mM/ug0354uxq/rR7eVf+QY1a6UKcv3W58nLZgd/VoHcnizbuk\nf0PYhjupWYnxjhZG2Gcy\n=lzFm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cde2e43a5035290940ad4ccba4296f2b4cb0ca59\nparent db3f4d7255b172950d346cba3d6c64c6c9f8c96a\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1781862966 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781862966 -0700\n\nchore(deps): bump js-yaml from 4.1.1 to 4.2.0 in /libs/cli/js-monorepo-example (#8143)\n\nBumps [js-yaml](https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml) from 4.1.1 to 4.2.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md\">js-yaml's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>[4.2.0] - 2026-06-01</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Added <code>docs/safety.md</code> with notes about processing\nuntrusted YAML.</li>\n<li>Added <code>maxDepth</code> (100) loader option. Not a problem, but\ngives a better\nexception instead of RangeError on stack overflow.</li>\n<li>Added <code>maxMergeSeqLength</code> (20) loader option. Not a\nproblem after <code>merge</code> fix,\nbut an additional restriction for safety.</li>\n<li>Added sourcemaps to <code>dist/</code> builds.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Changed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Stop resolving numbers with underscores as numeric scalars, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/issues/627\">#627</a>.</li>\n<li>Switched dev toolchains to Vite / neostandard.</li>\n<li>Updated demo.</li>\n<li>Reorganized tests.</li>\n<li><code>dist/</code> files are no longer kept in the repository.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Fixed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix parsing of properties on the first implicit block mapping key,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/issues/62\">#62</a>.</li>\n<li>Fix trailing whitespace handling when folding flow scalar lines, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/issues/307\">#307</a>.</li>\n<li>Reject top-level block scalars without content indentation, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/issues/280\">#280</a>.</li>\n<li>Ensure numbers survive round-trip, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/issues/737\">#737</a>.</li>\n<li>Fix test coverage for issue <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/issues/221\">#221</a>.</li>\n<li>Fix flow scalar trailing whitespace folding, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/issues/307\">#307</a>.</li>\n<li>Fix digits in YAML named tag handles.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Security</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix potential DoS via quadratic complexity in merge - deduplicate\nrepeated\nelements (makes sense for malformed files &gt; 10K).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[3.14.2] - 2025-11-15</h2>\n<h3>Security</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Backported v4.1.1 fix to v3</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commits\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=js-yaml&package-manager=npm_and_yarn&previous-version=4.1.1&new-version=4.2.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-19T09:56:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/c6eb0a20589d80e9b1964318c370a82f72889245","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/c6eb0a20589d80e9b1964318c370a82f72889245","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/c6eb0a20589d80e9b1964318c370a82f72889245/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"db3f4d7255b172950d346cba3d6c64c6c9f8c96a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/db3f4d7255b172950d346cba3d6c64c6c9f8c96a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/db3f4d7255b172950d346cba3d6c64c6c9f8c96a"}]},{"sha":"db3f4d7255b172950d346cba3d6c64c6c9f8c96a","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKGRiM2Y0ZDcyNTViMTcyOTUwZDM0NmNiYTNkNmM2NGM2YzlmOGM5NmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-19T08:34:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T08:34:16Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump bleach from 6.3.0 to 6.4.0 in /libs/langgraph (#8107)\n\nBumps [bleach](https://github.com/mozilla/bleach) from 6.3.0 to 6.4.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/blob/main/CHANGES\">bleach's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 6.4.0 (June 5th, 2026)</h2>\n<p><strong>NOTE: 2026-06-05: Bleach is no longer maintained. There will\nbe no future\nreleases including for security issues.</strong>\nSee issue:\n<code>&lt;https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/issues/698&gt;</code>__</p>\n<p><strong>Backwards incompatible changes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Dropped support for pypy 3.10. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/mozilla/bleach/issues/764\">#764</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Security fixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Fix bug 2023812 / GHSA-8rfp-98v4-mmr6.</p>\n<p>Fix XSS issue with sanitize_uri_value where disallowed schemes with\nUnicode invisible characters wouldn't be rejected.</p>\n<p>For example::</p>\n<p>import bleach\npayload1 = '<!-- raw HTML omitted -->Click<!-- raw HTML omitted -->'\nresult1 = bleach.clean(payload1)\nprint(repr(result1))</p>\n<p>outputs::</p>\n<p>'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->Click<!-- raw HTML omitted -->'</p>\n<p>See the advisory for details.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fix GHSA-gj48-438w-jh9v.</p>\n<p>Fix issue where URI sanitization wasn't happening in formaction\nattributes.</p>\n<p>See the advisory for details.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Bug fixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Add support for pypy 3.11. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/mozilla/bleach/issues/764\">#764</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Drop version max in tinycss2 pin. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/mozilla/bleach/issues/772\">#772</a>)</p>\n<p>This removes one of the things we had to keep checking and updating.\nUsers\nnow own the responsibility for correctness with the version of tinycss2\nthey're using.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/f0355a7af00500482c5292c6c83290c6a178068d\"><code>f0355a7</code></a>\nfix: fix last release date in CHANGES</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/ae4e8a26706516ad01b92e66321b480208a440da\"><code>ae4e8a2</code></a>\nchore: bleach 6.4.0 and final release</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/970df58e9f0c55cc52244f3f0106e473a40d886d\"><code>970df58</code></a>\nfix: uri-sanitization in formaction attributes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/7c4867c32344d1c961107fae62240a6f0dc680dc\"><code>7c4867c</code></a>\nfix: xss bypass in allowed protocol test using unicode invisible\ncharacters</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/913ab75992b845e2c9c060c41f24d46921db4693\"><code>913ab75</code></a>\nfix: reduce redundancy in workflow jobs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/218c15af455c8dec14f98fcb2e235f8680e93930\"><code>218c15a</code></a>\nfix: rework pip caching</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/4f0b097bf80548a022050e2f71f024d755a9f154\"><code>4f0b097</code></a>\nfix: fix tox platform restrictions</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/e95a79d07bb5d792425c2bc0ef5dd03f6614f3bb\"><code>e95a79d</code></a>\nchore: update pytest</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/91539d4e80d4685b8f2bedc79076ff0ff6c1b911\"><code>91539d4</code></a>\nBump actions/cache from 5.0.3 to 5.0.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/cd47b4ce495859065da23c2116f651e591e1e90d\"><code>cd47b4c</code></a>\nfix: handle left-angle-bracket that's not a tag (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/mozilla/bleach/issues/733\">#733</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/compare/v6.3.0...v6.4.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=bleach&package-manager=uv&previous-version=6.3.0&new-version=6.4.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8f6a0d7f6ec88223beee8cbacc2245ed183733b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/8f6a0d7f6ec88223beee8cbacc2245ed183733b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/db3f4d7255b172950d346cba3d6c64c6c9f8c96a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNP8ICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWQsQAFzhlG2WurOR0RkFhfZ50Duo\nJ5DtLs8y0L9cxO1qK0ZnoWwar/e6BNfhmyYg4GhVwFfrkw2RllPGH3e1sO9/rHSU\nqds4WphiZXUZ+MFPXMxJfZKkeRePv3nKQ4PYVQHKTivQ/T5N2ySbFFj5wF/Ej37S\nh9Q0L+/Sebi0r//2oDeUTrjuXgWOjWKRXag4JY980MXmMiTXWxcUIlHw3eGgqh66\nusKj4cIt8B4bmRjItikROzA5Bc6jsTfNU0nn07ysvg4cLTHJwQk0dmQn+lM/7Bq9\nmRGa0uaehHWssmHjwG4/j/xqRDnND+izv2KvNxx8QGrgiDIYEaPQ/NvozF42aycT\nPUFWsH0ndh/17l47MmH+YoQGf6+gtGLj4nQxr0wEydTYy/y9l3jEv4zmKDYNzmip\nWeRCBo0AtdN8Az9D6bTB9TR3TKWNBdhOMknNMi94yJ90dJyR5248Rbol7M+HOWQj\nyJ5apP9lGrvcHJmG8+8E2qwWEDgetaICGqsiT8V4GQ74BfEZEF7iM3x1iAFZy/TH\n/8ZSge1HQ5CGkn+OOdFKcr6BKb1l5jj8rCu8YQhSIrOUgXWktAwZkvegwCnBIKKZ\nLuS/nuBQkIZLYN2WxeCOgYTqmvAUACdaxYboApYRcz7TAgtl0JZIaHWKoffduo7V\nur9/hz6bMoGtZOZ0+lUZ\n=Ng2k\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8f6a0d7f6ec88223beee8cbacc2245ed183733b2\nparent 4401ae03e0d9117361163375597444f149d62fa5\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1781858056 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781858056 +0000\n\nchore(deps): bump bleach from 6.3.0 to 6.4.0 in /libs/langgraph (#8107)\n\nBumps [bleach](https://github.com/mozilla/bleach) from 6.3.0 to 6.4.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/blob/main/CHANGES\">bleach's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 6.4.0 (June 5th, 2026)</h2>\n<p><strong>NOTE: 2026-06-05: Bleach is no longer maintained. There will\nbe no future\nreleases including for security issues.</strong>\nSee issue:\n<code>&lt;https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/issues/698&gt;</code>__</p>\n<p><strong>Backwards incompatible changes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Dropped support for pypy 3.10. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/mozilla/bleach/issues/764\">#764</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Security fixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Fix bug 2023812 / GHSA-8rfp-98v4-mmr6.</p>\n<p>Fix XSS issue with sanitize_uri_value where disallowed schemes with\nUnicode invisible characters wouldn't be rejected.</p>\n<p>For example::</p>\n<p>import bleach\npayload1 = '<!-- raw HTML omitted -->Click<!-- raw HTML omitted -->'\nresult1 = bleach.clean(payload1)\nprint(repr(result1))</p>\n<p>outputs::</p>\n<p>'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->Click<!-- raw HTML omitted -->'</p>\n<p>See the advisory for details.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fix GHSA-gj48-438w-jh9v.</p>\n<p>Fix issue where URI sanitization wasn't happening in formaction\nattributes.</p>\n<p>See the advisory for details.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Bug fixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Add support for pypy 3.11. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/mozilla/bleach/issues/764\">#764</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Drop version max in tinycss2 pin. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/mozilla/bleach/issues/772\">#772</a>)</p>\n<p>This removes one of the things we had to keep checking and updating.\nUsers\nnow own the responsibility for correctness with the version of tinycss2\nthey're using.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/f0355a7af00500482c5292c6c83290c6a178068d\"><code>f0355a7</code></a>\nfix: fix last release date in CHANGES</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/ae4e8a26706516ad01b92e66321b480208a440da\"><code>ae4e8a2</code></a>\nchore: bleach 6.4.0 and final release</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/970df58e9f0c55cc52244f3f0106e473a40d886d\"><code>970df58</code></a>\nfix: uri-sanitization in formaction attributes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/7c4867c32344d1c961107fae62240a6f0dc680dc\"><code>7c4867c</code></a>\nfix: xss bypass in allowed protocol test using unicode invisible\ncharacters</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/913ab75992b845e2c9c060c41f24d46921db4693\"><code>913ab75</code></a>\nfix: reduce redundancy in workflow jobs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/218c15af455c8dec14f98fcb2e235f8680e93930\"><code>218c15a</code></a>\nfix: rework pip caching</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/4f0b097bf80548a022050e2f71f024d755a9f154\"><code>4f0b097</code></a>\nfix: fix tox platform restrictions</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/e95a79d07bb5d792425c2bc0ef5dd03f6614f3bb\"><code>e95a79d</code></a>\nchore: update pytest</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/91539d4e80d4685b8f2bedc79076ff0ff6c1b911\"><code>91539d4</code></a>\nBump actions/cache from 5.0.3 to 5.0.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/commit/cd47b4ce495859065da23c2116f651e591e1e90d\"><code>cd47b4c</code></a>\nfix: handle left-angle-bracket that's not a tag (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/mozilla/bleach/issues/733\">#733</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mozilla/bleach/compare/v6.3.0...v6.4.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=bleach&package-manager=uv&previous-version=6.3.0&new-version=6.4.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-19T08:34:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/db3f4d7255b172950d346cba3d6c64c6c9f8c96a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/db3f4d7255b172950d346cba3d6c64c6c9f8c96a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/db3f4d7255b172950d346cba3d6c64c6c9f8c96a/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4401ae03e0d9117361163375597444f149d62fa5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/4401ae03e0d9117361163375597444f149d62fa5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/4401ae03e0d9117361163375597444f149d62fa5"}]},{"sha":"4401ae03e0d9117361163375597444f149d62fa5","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKDQ0MDFhZTAzZTBkOTExNzM2MTE2MzM3NTU5NzQ0NGYxNDlkNjJmYTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-19T08:33:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T08:33:28Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump cryptography from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1 in /libs/langgraph (#8106)\n\nBumps [cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography) from 46.0.7\nto 48.0.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:</p>\n<p>48.0.0 - 2026-05-04<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Support for Python 3.8 has\nbeen removed.\n<code>cryptography</code> now requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Loading an X.509 CRL whose\ninner\n<code>TBSCertList.signature</code> algorithm does not match the outer\n<code>signatureAlgorithm</code> now raises <code>ValueError</code>.\nPreviously, such CRLs\nwere parsed successfully and only rejected during signature\nvalidation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added support for\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mlkem</code> and\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mldsa</code> when using OpenSSL\n3.5.0 or\nlater, in addition to the existing AWS-LC and BoringSSL support. This\nmeans\npost-quantum algorithms are now available to users of our wheels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> Going forward, we do not guarantee that all\nfunctionality\nin <code>cryptography</code> will be available when building against\nOpenSSL. See :doc:<code>/statements/state-of-openssl</code> for more\ninformation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. _v47-0-0:</p>\n<p>47.0.0 - 2026-04-24</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Support for Python 3.8 is deprecated and will be removed in the next\n  ``cryptography`` release.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for binary elliptic curves\n  (``SECT*`` classes) has been removed. These curves are rarely used and\n  have additional security considerations that make them undesirable.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for OpenSSL 1.1.x has been\nremoved.\nOpenSSL 3.0.0 or later is now required. LibreSSL, BoringSSL, and AWS-LC\n  continue to be supported.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Dropped support for LibreSSL &lt; 4.1.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Loading keys with unsupported algorithms\nor\n  keys with unsupported explicit curve encodings now raises\n  :class:`~cryptography.exceptions.UnsupportedAlgorithm` instead of\n  ``ValueError``. This change affects\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_public_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_public_key`,\n  and :meth:`~cryptography.x509.Certificate.public_key` when called on\n  certificates with unsupported public key algorithms.\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/8e03e30e3aae01632a697e903e3593c924f0139d\"><code>8e03e30</code></a>\nbump for 48.0.0 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14796\">#14796</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/295e0d254ef31ab864730aa41312ec355416ee71\"><code>295e0d2</code></a>\nAdd AGENTS.md with CLAUDE.md symlink (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14794\">#14794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/104a2de19e268a433e6da92be9cb872dcf0003c8\"><code>104a2de</code></a>\nBump BoringSSL, OpenSSL, AWS-LC in CI (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14793\">#14793</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/67ec1e51988195e17993d2edef5258b27509b926\"><code>67ec1e5</code></a>\ncall check_length early on AesSiv::encrypt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14792\">#14792</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/b2da57a0d9e4bfd2b95364299091a18f74127b26\"><code>b2da57a</code></a>\nchangelog for mldsa/mlkem for openssl (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14791\">#14791</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/3cf44adee25c368d4a136e072fa9f80465d91eb0\"><code>3cf44ad</code></a>\nML-KEM OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14781\">#14781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e31639666766f846fbab2c605879db0fa64fe83\"><code>2e31639</code></a>\nML-DSA OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14773\">#14773</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/5affe5a286a986fdf512c4a5cb280d28a96c10e3\"><code>5affe5a</code></a>\nfix rust nightly clippy (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14790\">#14790</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e73ca448eaf64b6f0d4ffbb794cf96170cef5ec\"><code>2e73ca4</code></a>\nbump rust-openssl dep and update EcPoint::mul_generator to\nmul_generator2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/1\">#1</a>...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/46.0.7...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=cryptography&package-manager=uv&previous-version=46.0.7&new-version=48.0.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"754573eead68eb845d7e25b5cc3199d8914cf2db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/754573eead68eb845d7e25b5cc3199d8914cf2db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/4401ae03e0d9117361163375597444f149d62fa5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNP7YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfwAQAHYBPIss09HEod2CStz1264v\nKF5ixxJKqxQqG71s2UShu1So/Ouqy5SjOLP1y0pT6+T7ABU8KTyJyo43/iHk9Hzj\n+Z+nxi2zc/6UDNhwOM2owWdPH7LcoLMDJXqJTp4z6YlroVoJRGimAgMS7SE9+BBC\n1v1xFSSRyxauzN35I74bZVwHEr19HxKXUg1lR6SJPggCN/3FGhu763lDsHpWRlYp\nPu9xU+U76MM1AfzIcuIU+Fn2vZ5A7uWv+mmxIh7XON3Kec1I6afKqAPQEVd77Fhf\nscCNk0iw5ZhfILJj7KuME9nrkYtBHkOwvbAxHJPKdUuaT6y1odHEgCAx0LRG4/3+\nP9T5dMLgOUXNoFWPKcq+2gkpgIlecFFNfwXhdHn/Gljy2AORD6lOeYxenWFFh0PH\nkUqjs/SwQ/CYJ87IVOD2dvL2MhwRPVd+rt05mKLAnyJUsKle3m9zvhS2PVa5Fhfs\nSLNpVBd0CS5RweNSko/1ULATPKhvsgaxQdo4tYqXFu9S5dhT4kACi1bPh9DLYmKP\nIKP9aeaqPCvE1YCdL94jxZpqLRq/DVQuOs2dzWsm/TsLzVmicr8w452szLnmvRiz\nuKHwAtVsI0HNFYTE6vL8dr7Ao0KJO4HSSOfJKqa0y8NTviIJhJGDkyZwsTSfPJyn\nliMTIpuZNAskewS0f3kP\n=my5Z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 754573eead68eb845d7e25b5cc3199d8914cf2db\nparent 871d6fc804cd6f77f4392aa81cf51101e5c63e14\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1781858008 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781858008 +0000\n\nchore(deps): bump cryptography from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1 in /libs/langgraph (#8106)\n\nBumps [cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography) from 46.0.7\nto 48.0.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:</p>\n<p>48.0.0 - 2026-05-04<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Support for Python 3.8 has\nbeen removed.\n<code>cryptography</code> now requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Loading an X.509 CRL whose\ninner\n<code>TBSCertList.signature</code> algorithm does not match the outer\n<code>signatureAlgorithm</code> now raises <code>ValueError</code>.\nPreviously, such CRLs\nwere parsed successfully and only rejected during signature\nvalidation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added support for\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mlkem</code> and\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mldsa</code> when using OpenSSL\n3.5.0 or\nlater, in addition to the existing AWS-LC and BoringSSL support. This\nmeans\npost-quantum algorithms are now available to users of our wheels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> Going forward, we do not guarantee that all\nfunctionality\nin <code>cryptography</code> will be available when building against\nOpenSSL. See :doc:<code>/statements/state-of-openssl</code> for more\ninformation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. _v47-0-0:</p>\n<p>47.0.0 - 2026-04-24</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Support for Python 3.8 is deprecated and will be removed in the next\n  ``cryptography`` release.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for binary elliptic curves\n  (``SECT*`` classes) has been removed. These curves are rarely used and\n  have additional security considerations that make them undesirable.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for OpenSSL 1.1.x has been\nremoved.\nOpenSSL 3.0.0 or later is now required. LibreSSL, BoringSSL, and AWS-LC\n  continue to be supported.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Dropped support for LibreSSL &lt; 4.1.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Loading keys with unsupported algorithms\nor\n  keys with unsupported explicit curve encodings now raises\n  :class:`~cryptography.exceptions.UnsupportedAlgorithm` instead of\n  ``ValueError``. This change affects\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_public_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_public_key`,\n  and :meth:`~cryptography.x509.Certificate.public_key` when called on\n  certificates with unsupported public key algorithms.\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/8e03e30e3aae01632a697e903e3593c924f0139d\"><code>8e03e30</code></a>\nbump for 48.0.0 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14796\">#14796</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/295e0d254ef31ab864730aa41312ec355416ee71\"><code>295e0d2</code></a>\nAdd AGENTS.md with CLAUDE.md symlink (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14794\">#14794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/104a2de19e268a433e6da92be9cb872dcf0003c8\"><code>104a2de</code></a>\nBump BoringSSL, OpenSSL, AWS-LC in CI (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14793\">#14793</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/67ec1e51988195e17993d2edef5258b27509b926\"><code>67ec1e5</code></a>\ncall check_length early on AesSiv::encrypt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14792\">#14792</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/b2da57a0d9e4bfd2b95364299091a18f74127b26\"><code>b2da57a</code></a>\nchangelog for mldsa/mlkem for openssl (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14791\">#14791</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/3cf44adee25c368d4a136e072fa9f80465d91eb0\"><code>3cf44ad</code></a>\nML-KEM OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14781\">#14781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e31639666766f846fbab2c605879db0fa64fe83\"><code>2e31639</code></a>\nML-DSA OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14773\">#14773</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/5affe5a286a986fdf512c4a5cb280d28a96c10e3\"><code>5affe5a</code></a>\nfix rust nightly clippy (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14790\">#14790</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e73ca448eaf64b6f0d4ffbb794cf96170cef5ec\"><code>2e73ca4</code></a>\nbump rust-openssl dep and update EcPoint::mul_generator to\nmul_generator2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/1\">#1</a>...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/46.0.7...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=cryptography&package-manager=uv&previous-version=46.0.7&new-version=48.0.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-19T08:33:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/4401ae03e0d9117361163375597444f149d62fa5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/4401ae03e0d9117361163375597444f149d62fa5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/4401ae03e0d9117361163375597444f149d62fa5/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VX