it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-19T08:28:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/510d943362a7fde63a74855ac51418d6f1bc3768","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/510d943362a7fde63a74855ac51418d6f1bc3768","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/510d943362a7fde63a74855ac51418d6f1bc3768/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a4157ef280b236aecc331a7a17d7695d9e0e95e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/a4157ef280b236aecc331a7a17d7695d9e0e95e9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/a4157ef280b236aecc331a7a17d7695d9e0e95e9"}]},{"sha":"a4157ef280b236aecc331a7a17d7695d9e0e95e9","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKGE0MTU3ZWYyODBiMjM2YWVjYzMzMWE3YTE3ZDc2OTVkOWUwZTk1ZTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-19T08:25:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T08:25:58Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump pyjwt from 2.12.0 to 2.13.0 in /libs/langgraph (#8092)\n\nBumps [pyjwt](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt) from 2.12.0 to 2.13.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/releases\">pyjwt's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.13.0</h2>\n<h1>PyJWT 2.13.0 — Security Release</h1>\n<p>This release bundles five security fixes plus three additional\nhardening / spec-compliance changes. We recommend all users upgrade.</p>\n<h2>Security</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\"><code>GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx</code></a>\n— JWK JSON accepted as HMAC secret (algorithm confusion).</strong>\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> previously rejected PEM- and\nSSH-formatted asymmetric keys but did not catch a JWK passed as a raw\nJSON string. In a verifier configured with both symmetric and asymmetric\nalgorithms in <code>algorithms=[…]</code> and a raw-JSON JWK as the key,\nan attacker could forge HS256 tokens using the JWK text as the HMAC\nsecret. The guard has been extended to reject any JWK-shaped JSON.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aradona91\"><code>@​aradona91</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\"><code>GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f</code></a>\n— Algorithm allow-list bypass with <code>PyJWK</code> /\n<code>PyJWKClient</code>.</strong> When verifying with a\n<code>PyJWK</code>, the caller's <code>algorithms=[…]</code> allow-list\nwas checked against the token header <code>alg</code> as a string only;\nactual verification used the algorithm bound to the <code>PyJWK</code>.\nAn attacker who controlled a registered JWKS key could sign with one\nalgorithm and advertise another on the header. PyJWT now requires the\ntoken header <code>alg</code> to match the <code>PyJWK</code>'s\nalgorithm before verification. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sushi-gif\"><code>@​sushi-gif</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\"><code>GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39</code></a>\n— DoS via base64 decode of unused payload segment when\n<code>b64=false</code>.</strong> For detached-payload JWS\n(<code>b64=false</code>), the compact-form payload segment was\nbase64-decoded before being discarded in favor of the caller-supplied\n<code>detached_payload</code>. An attacker could inflate the unused\nsegment to force CPU + memory cost without holding a valid signature.\nThe segment is now required to be empty per RFC 7515 Appendix F, and is\nno longer decoded. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/thesmartshadow\"><code>@​thesmartshadow</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\"><code>GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> accepts non-HTTP(S) URIs.</strong>\n<code>PyJWKClient.fetch_data</code> passed its URI to\n<code>urllib.request.urlopen</code>, which by default also handles\n<code>file://</code>, <code>ftp://</code>, and <code>data:</code>\nschemes. An application that fed an attacker-influenced URI into\n<code>PyJWKClient</code> could be coerced into reading local files or\nreaching other unintended schemes. <code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects\nany URI whose scheme isn't <code>http</code> or <code>https</code>.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KEIJOT\"><code>@​KEIJOT</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\"><code>GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> cache wiped on fetch error.</strong> A\n<code>finally</code>-block <code>put(jwk_set=None)</code> cleared the\nJWK Set cache whenever a fetch raised, turning a transient JWKS-endpoint\noutage into application-wide auth failure. The cache write was moved\ninto the success path; transient errors no longer evict valid cached\nkeys. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/eddieran\"><code>@​eddieran</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Fixed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reject empty HMAC keys outright in\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> with <code>InvalidKeyError</code>\ninstead of accepting them with only a warning. Defends against the\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code> footgun.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/SnailSploit\"><code>@​SnailSploit</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/spartan8806\"><code>@​spartan8806</code></a>\nfor the reports.</em></li>\n<li>Forward per-call <code>options</code> (including\n<code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code>) from <code>PyJWT.decode</code>\nthrough to <code>PyJWS._verify_signature</code>. The option was\npreviously silently dropped between the two layers, so it only took\neffect when set on the <code>PyJWT</code> instance. <em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WLUB\"><code>@​WLUB</code></a> for the\nreport.</em></li>\n<li><strong>RFC 7797 §3 compliance for <code>b64=false</code>:</strong>\nthe encoder now auto-adds <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> to\n<code>crit</code>, and the decoder rejects tokens that set\n<code>b64=false</code> without listing it in <code>crit</code>.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/MachineLearning-Nerd\"><code>@​MachineLearning-Nerd</code></a>\nfor the report.</em></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups, by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152\">#1152</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Upgrade notes</h2>\n<p>Most fixes are invisible to correctly-configured callers. A few\nbehavioral changes you may encounter:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Empty HMAC keys now raise.</strong> If your app passed\n<code>&quot;&quot;</code> or <code>b&quot;&quot;</code> as a secret\n(often via a missing env var, e.g.\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code>),\n<code>encode</code>/<code>decode</code> will now raise\n<code>InvalidKeyError</code>. This is the intended behavior — fix the\nconfiguration.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWK</code> decoding now requires the token's\n<code>alg</code> to match the JWK's algorithm.</strong> Previously a\nmismatch was silently honored if the header <code>alg</code> appeared in\nthe allow-list. Tokens that relied on this mismatch will now fail with\n<code>InvalidAlgorithmError</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects non-HTTP(S) URIs at\nconstruction time.</strong> Tests or dev environments that fetched JWKS\nfrom <code>file://</code> URIs need to switch to a local HTTP server or\nload the JWKS by other means (e.g. construct\n<code>PyJWKSet.from_dict(...)</code> directly).</li>\n<li><strong><code>b64=false</code> tokens are now strictly RFC 7515 /\n7797 compliant.</strong> Tokens with a non-empty compact-form payload\nsegment, or that omit <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> from\n<code>crit</code>, will be rejected. PyJWT-produced tokens always\nsatisfy both invariants, so round-trips through PyJWT are\nunaffected.</li>\n<li><strong><code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code> set per-call now\ntakes effect.</strong> Callers who passed\n<code>options={&quot;enforce_minimum_key_length&quot;: True}</code> to\n<code>jwt.decode()</code> previously got no enforcement; they will now\nget <code>InvalidKeyError</code> on undersized keys, as documented.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full changelog:</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0</a></p>\n<h2>2.12.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add typing_extensions dependency for Python &lt; 3.11 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla\"><code>@​jpadilla</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1151\">jpadilla/pyjwt#1151</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.0...2.12.1\">https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.0...2.12.1</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/blob/master/CHANGELOG.rst\">pyjwt's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><code>v2.13.0\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0&gt;</code>__</h2>\n<p>Security</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject JWK JSON documents passed as raw HMAC secrets in\n  ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` to close an algorithm-confusion gap that\n  the existing PEM/SSH guard did not cover. Reported by @aradona91 in\n`GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx&gt;`__.\n- Bind the JWT header ``alg`` to ``PyJWK.algorithm_name`` during\n  verification so the caller's ``algorithms=[...]`` allow-list cannot be\nbypassed when decoding with a ``PyJWK`` / ``PyJWKClient`` key. Reported\nby @sushi-gif in `GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f&gt;`__.\n- Reject non-``http(s)`` URI schemes in ``PyJWKClient`` so attacker-\ninfluenced URIs cannot read local files or reach unintended schemes via\nurllib's default ``file://`` / ``ftp://`` / ``data:`` handlers. Reported\nby @KEIJOT in `GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4&gt;`__.\n- Preserve the cached JWK Set on fetch errors in\n``PyJWKClient.fetch_data``.\n  The previous ``finally``-block ``put(None)`` pattern cleared the cache\non any transient outage, turning one bad JWKS request into application-\nwide auth failure. Reported by @eddieran in `GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8&gt;`__.\n- Skip the unconditional base64 decode of the compact-form payload\nsegment\n  when ``b64=false`` is set in the protected header, and require that\n  segment to be empty (RFC 7515 Appendix F detached form). Closes an\n  unauthenticated DoS amplifier. Reported by @thesmartshadow in\n`GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39&gt;`__.\n<p>Fixed</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject empty HMAC keys outright in ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` with\n  ``InvalidKeyError`` instead of accepting them with only a warning.\n  Thanks to @SnailSploit and @spartan8806 for independently flagging the\n  footgun.\n- Forward per-call ``options`` (including\n``enforce_minimum_key_length``)\n  from ``PyJWT.decode`` through to ``PyJWS._verify_signature`` so the\noption actually takes effect when set at the call site rather than only\n  on the ``PyJWT`` instance. Thanks to @WLUB for the report.\n- RFC 7797 §3 compliance for ``b64=false``: the encoder now auto-adds\n``&amp;quot;b64&amp;quot;`` to the ``crit`` header parameter, and the\ndecoder rejects\ntokens that set ``b64=false`` without listing it in ``crit``. Thanks to\n  @MachineLearning-Nerd for the report.\n\nChanged\n</code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in\n<code>[#1152](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152)\n&amp;lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152&amp;gt;</code>__</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>v2.12.1\n&amp;lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.0...2.12.1&amp;gt;</code>__\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;\n</code></pre></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/7144e4534c34810f4525dc4578a32addd8212cff\"><code>7144e45</code></a>\nApply ruff format</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/d2f4bec4963897c0ef96ef64a875894f2c8542ab\"><code>d2f4bec</code></a>\nRestore <code>cast()</code> calls with cross-version <code>type:\nignore</code> for <code>prepare_key</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/22f478cebddd8294259c30f037ecb92b0b348774\"><code>22f478c</code></a>\nRemove redundant casts in <code>RSAAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> and\n`ECAlgorithm.prepare...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/95791b1759b8aa4f2203575d344d5c78564cdc81\"><code>95791b1</code></a>\nBundle security fixes and hardening into 2.13.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/dcc27a9d3182a2349c30b160758785c6ce7a6508\"><code>dcc27a9</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1155\">#1155</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/9d08a9a1896845ed8eaf88e6f6ac61e5800c3e7a\"><code>9d08a9a</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1146\">#1146</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/b87c10014d4109f0214fea188d00faaaf8a80e64\"><code>b87c100</code></a>\nBump codecov/codecov-action from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1154\">#1154</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/40e3147eb5f790d8d041772e5fc00728a176c812\"><code>40e3147</code></a>\nMigrate development extras to dependency groups (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152\">#1152</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/a4e1a3d1218b01c5806420b8f16d9308ac4adc30\"><code>a4e1a3d</code></a>\nAdd typing_extensions dependency for Python &lt; 3.11 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1151\">#1151</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.0...2.13.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=pyjwt&package-manager=uv&previous-version=2.12.0&new-version=2.13.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"96a7379a4b87a6de46f5cf9a9d10ac40f2812d98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/96a7379a4b87a6de46f5cf9a9d10ac40f2812d98"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/a4157ef280b236aecc331a7a17d7695d9e0e95e9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNP0WCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABhQQAGVD5jegpzb6f0acsPPKQcNe\nGiFu1Kt/tf3ASsLfx76bTmnoHoMjct0xGPYwAULNgxBhr4VyH8jpZTadEIk7VnHu\n/QC22jbR4nkbHKSzo1+egBloD1IUykxIveQMv0fs8P703VF1FwQvmAdQU0SUFQJX\nDUl3v0NNvivMWsxRFAEAhKWwccMTZH27CfsJz0h9LAhB2Zr4SvkRQ7TGOl6s+Xi8\n0SayU9qM4JuAV+OlByg54n9BpFDW5xaaA/LolbuNPqoHmcAStRKrj6p6PxaQCacK\n3PQTOtwqjEnszTr0souW05ri9hlAuO3ve9GtW6lAL+t6Tw7QBBxv4OBwPnnqTT9X\nYZIjYmazU9/RkxyBxT4rObpIrlVMutNw85jqJKMqq748A1iZ7FFNZxrS7VrcgAKn\n9TAKF6a/3jMCd4A6ouQRcCl2gfoZjI7JFyrDBWtN+R/lgVy+kDL6/ORi+ZaQ3gdQ\nzsjzL8NZeolz37S86UxUEFHXf8xUVME3mb0FfFJQXdsT1v9vXoEPyxVfNmsNF0kx\nBxkN7tZWcIqk6hU4F3jJ0row53ruV46BAloJOAphEeMbINpbAAJMKr1AKMO/nMNS\nuP1pb2SQ4Z8jrIy5CXDVt7th/ZsEpi0bFgNSUiaGvs2QRxUn+zMaRUtjXW3Wdcps\nTHWECrd5hy5ve/jmpeCy\n=L5/Z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 96a7379a4b87a6de46f5cf9a9d10ac40f2812d98\nparent ce6c8b2410f9921d379c8fe8ea8087d1934c07a9\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1781857558 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781857558 -0700\n\nchore(deps): bump pyjwt from 2.12.0 to 2.13.0 in /libs/langgraph (#8092)\n\nBumps [pyjwt](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt) from 2.12.0 to 2.13.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/releases\">pyjwt's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.13.0</h2>\n<h1>PyJWT 2.13.0 — Security Release</h1>\n<p>This release bundles five security fixes plus three additional\nhardening / spec-compliance changes. We recommend all users upgrade.</p>\n<h2>Security</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\"><code>GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx</code></a>\n— JWK JSON accepted as HMAC secret (algorithm confusion).</strong>\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> previously rejected PEM- and\nSSH-formatted asymmetric keys but did not catch a JWK passed as a raw\nJSON string. In a verifier configured with both symmetric and asymmetric\nalgorithms in <code>algorithms=[…]</code> and a raw-JSON JWK as the key,\nan attacker could forge HS256 tokens using the JWK text as the HMAC\nsecret. The guard has been extended to reject any JWK-shaped JSON.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aradona91\"><code>@​aradona91</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\"><code>GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f</code></a>\n— Algorithm allow-list bypass with <code>PyJWK</code> /\n<code>PyJWKClient</code>.</strong> When verifying with a\n<code>PyJWK</code>, the caller's <code>algorithms=[…]</code> allow-list\nwas checked against the token header <code>alg</code> as a string only;\nactual verification used the algorithm bound to the <code>PyJWK</code>.\nAn attacker who controlled a registered JWKS key could sign with one\nalgorithm and advertise another on the header. PyJWT now requires the\ntoken header <code>alg</code> to match the <code>PyJWK</code>'s\nalgorithm before verification. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sushi-gif\"><code>@​sushi-gif</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\"><code>GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39</code></a>\n— DoS via base64 decode of unused payload segment when\n<code>b64=false</code>.</strong> For detached-payload JWS\n(<code>b64=false</code>), the compact-form payload segment was\nbase64-decoded before being discarded in favor of the caller-supplied\n<code>detached_payload</code>. An attacker could inflate the unused\nsegment to force CPU + memory cost without holding a valid signature.\nThe segment is now required to be empty per RFC 7515 Appendix F, and is\nno longer decoded. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/thesmartshadow\"><code>@​thesmartshadow</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\"><code>GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> accepts non-HTTP(S) URIs.</strong>\n<code>PyJWKClient.fetch_data</code> passed its URI to\n<code>urllib.request.urlopen</code>, which by default also handles\n<code>file://</code>, <code>ftp://</code>, and <code>data:</code>\nschemes. An application that fed an attacker-influenced URI into\n<code>PyJWKClient</code> could be coerced into reading local files or\nreaching other unintended schemes. <code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects\nany URI whose scheme isn't <code>http</code> or <code>https</code>.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KEIJOT\"><code>@​KEIJOT</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\"><code>GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> cache wiped on fetch error.</strong> A\n<code>finally</code>-block <code>put(jwk_set=None)</code> cleared the\nJWK Set cache whenever a fetch raised, turning a transient JWKS-endpoint\noutage into application-wide auth failure. The cache write was moved\ninto the success path; transient errors no longer evict valid cached\nkeys. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/eddieran\"><code>@​eddieran</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Fixed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reject empty HMAC keys outright in\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> with <code>InvalidKeyError</code>\ninstead of accepting them with only a warning. Defends against the\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code> footgun.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/SnailSploit\"><code>@​SnailSploit</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/spartan8806\"><code>@​spartan8806</code></a>\nfor the reports.</em></li>\n<li>Forward per-call <code>options</code> (including\n<code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code>) from <code>PyJWT.decode</code>\nthrough to <code>PyJWS._verify_signature</code>. The option was\npreviously silently dropped between the two layers, so it only took\neffect when set on the <code>PyJWT</code> instance. <em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WLUB\"><code>@​WLUB</code></a> for the\nreport.</em></li>\n<li><strong>RFC 7797 §3 compliance for <code>b64=false</code>:</strong>\nthe encoder now auto-adds <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> to\n<code>crit</code>, and the decoder rejects tokens that set\n<code>b64=false</code> without listing it in <code>crit</code>.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/MachineLearning-Nerd\"><code>@​MachineLearning-Nerd</code></a>\nfor the report.</em></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups, by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152\">#1152</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Upgrade notes</h2>\n<p>Most fixes are invisible to correctly-configured callers. A few\nbehavioral changes you may encounter:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Empty HMAC keys now raise.</strong> If your app passed\n<code>&quot;&quot;</code> or <code>b&quot;&quot;</code> as a secret\n(often via a missing env var, e.g.\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code>),\n<code>encode</code>/<code>decode</code> will now raise\n<code>InvalidKeyError</code>. This is the intended behavior — fix the\nconfiguration.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWK</code> decoding now requires the token's\n<code>alg</code> to match the JWK's algorithm.</strong> Previously a\nmismatch was silently honored if the header <code>alg</code> appeared in\nthe allow-list. Tokens that relied on this mismatch will now fail with\n<code>InvalidAlgorithmError</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects non-HTTP(S) URIs at\nconstruction time.</strong> Tests or dev environments that fetched JWKS\nfrom <code>file://</code> URIs need to switch to a local HTTP server or\nload the JWKS by other means (e.g. construct\n<code>PyJWKSet.from_dict(...)</code> directly).</li>\n<li><strong><code>b64=false</code> tokens are now strictly RFC 7515 /\n7797 compliant.</strong> Tokens with a non-empty compact-form payload\nsegment, or that omit <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> from\n<code>crit</code>, will be rejected. PyJWT-produced tokens always\nsatisfy both invariants, so round-trips through PyJWT are\nunaffected.</li>\n<li><strong><code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code> set per-call now\ntakes effect.</strong> Callers who passed\n<code>options={&quot;enforce_minimum_key_length&quot;: True}</code> to\n<code>jwt.decode()</code> previously got no enforcement; they will now\nget <code>InvalidKeyError</code> on undersized keys, as documented.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full changelog:</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0</a></p>\n<h2>2.12.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add typing_extensions dependency for Python &lt; 3.11 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla\"><code>@​jpadilla</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1151\">jpadilla/pyjwt#1151</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.0...2.12.1\">https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.0...2.12.1</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/blob/master/CHANGELOG.rst\">pyjwt's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><code>v2.13.0\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0&gt;</code>__</h2>\n<p>Security</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject JWK JSON documents passed as raw HMAC secrets in\n  ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` to close an algorithm-confusion gap that\n  the existing PEM/SSH guard did not cover. Reported by @aradona91 in\n`GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx&gt;`__.\n- Bind the JWT header ``alg`` to ``PyJWK.algorithm_name`` during\n  verification so the caller's ``algorithms=[...]`` allow-list cannot be\nbypassed when decoding with a ``PyJWK`` / ``PyJWKClient`` key. Reported\nby @sushi-gif in `GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f&gt;`__.\n- Reject non-``http(s)`` URI schemes in ``PyJWKClient`` so attacker-\ninfluenced URIs cannot read local files or reach unintended schemes via\nurllib's default ``file://`` / ``ftp://`` / ``data:`` handlers. Reported\nby @KEIJOT in `GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4&gt;`__.\n- Preserve the cached JWK Set on fetch errors in\n``PyJWKClient.fetch_data``.\n  The previous ``finally``-block ``put(None)`` pattern cleared the cache\non any transient outage, turning one bad JWKS request into application-\nwide auth failure. Reported by @eddieran in `GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8&gt;`__.\n- Skip the unconditional base64 decode of the compact-form payload\nsegment\n  when ``b64=false`` is set in the protected header, and require that\n  segment to be empty (RFC 7515 Appendix F detached form). Closes an\n  unauthenticated DoS amplifier. Reported by @thesmartshadow in\n`GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39&gt;`__.\n<p>Fixed</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject empty HMAC keys outright in ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` with\n  ``InvalidKeyError`` instead of accepting them with only a warning.\n  Thanks to @SnailSploit and @spartan8806 for independently flagging the\n  footgun.\n- Forward per-call ``options`` (including\n``enforce_minimum_key_length``)\n  from ``PyJWT.decode`` through to ``PyJWS._verify_signature`` so the\noption actually takes effect when set at the call site rather than only\n  on the ``PyJWT`` instance. Thanks to @WLUB for the report.\n- RFC 7797 §3 compliance for ``b64=false``: the encoder now auto-adds\n``&amp;quot;b64&amp;quot;`` to the ``crit`` header parameter, and the\ndecoder rejects\ntokens that set ``b64=false`` without listing it in ``crit``. Thanks to\n  @MachineLearning-Nerd for the report.\n\nChanged\n</code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in\n<code>[#1152](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152)\n&amp;lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152&amp;gt;</code>__</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>v2.12.1\n&amp;lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.0...2.12.1&amp;gt;</code>__\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;\n</code></pre></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/7144e4534c34810f4525dc4578a32addd8212cff\"><code>7144e45</code></a>\nApply ruff format</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/d2f4bec4963897c0ef96ef64a875894f2c8542ab\"><code>d2f4bec</code></a>\nRestore <code>cast()</code> calls with cross-version <code>type:\nignore</code> for <code>prepare_key</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/22f478cebddd8294259c30f037ecb92b0b348774\"><code>22f478c</code></a>\nRemove redundant casts in <code>RSAAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> and\n`ECAlgorithm.prepare...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/95791b1759b8aa4f2203575d344d5c78564cdc81\"><code>95791b1</code></a>\nBundle security fixes and hardening into 2.13.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/dcc27a9d3182a2349c30b160758785c6ce7a6508\"><code>dcc27a9</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1155\">#1155</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/9d08a9a1896845ed8eaf88e6f6ac61e5800c3e7a\"><code>9d08a9a</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1146\">#1146</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/b87c10014d4109f0214fea188d00faaaf8a80e64\"><code>b87c100</code></a>\nBump codecov/codecov-action from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1154\">#1154</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/40e3147eb5f790d8d041772e5fc00728a176c812\"><code>40e3147</code></a>\nMigrate development extras to dependency groups (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152\">#1152</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/a4e1a3d1218b01c5806420b8f16d9308ac4adc30\"><code>a4e1a3d</code></a>\nAdd typing_extensions dependency for Python &lt; 3.11 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1151\">#1151</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.0...2.13.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=pyjwt&package-manager=uv&previous-version=2.12.0&new-version=2.13.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-19T08:25:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/a4157ef280b236aecc331a7a17d7695d9e0e95e9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/a4157ef280b236aecc331a7a17d7695d9e0e95e9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/a4157ef280b236aecc331a7a17d7695d9e0e95e9/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ce6c8b2410f9921d379c8fe8ea8087d1934c07a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/ce6c8b2410f9921d379c8fe8ea8087d1934c07a9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/ce6c8b2410f9921d379c8fe8ea8087d1934c07a9"}]},{"sha":"ce6c8b2410f9921d379c8fe8ea8087d1934c07a9","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKGNlNmM4YjI0MTBmOTkyMWQzNzljOGZlOGVhODA4N2QxOTM0YzA3YTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-18T20:53:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T20:53:47Z"},"message":"release(langgraph): 1.2.6 (#8139)","tree":{"sha":"220d08690e900748bcb99ab3a7df68ff143f2cc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/220d08690e900748bcb99ab3a7df68ff143f2cc4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/ce6c8b2410f9921d379c8fe8ea8087d1934c07a9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNFrbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApBgQAGglB10NhuO7YV5MpDDbm+pX\nbxjzhmdcWeFMdUJv1zizVYzmzxNKCoXDKI/bp0KZ2XPNXjL+EsMHPlrSr64mSMtL\nh1vGIqoMEFpeUyEEFViaPrfrHOfmDenV6AoyJ0yM6wmKmCAyoNBO0tQDWTFtfNDb\nTYMvsiJjPDtG5ECDX1hOK1B3Lw00fGS9cbfyV9AFge8+S0zGVhLogCIS7acOMFeP\nf3KysxWNDqkDjbwl5KVUJyifP0YXuyKnJ6nSDb7DHEfVvus051sF2rK7/aFgFWIa\nhXC60NMK4M7VOYAed2bp1qvvl3YQX7VxMgGXrmr4dcUYRnZGtnNg1SGrGYh2JAca\nkDfKgrEeSdjs+cjml1KQZAgCeRnBdmGXiqCeEt+20AkzO4G4hnIV1a9SDukeeaQq\nnw2zV+N1scfrBSLCfiUiSNsuixyN5DdBWJ+uCKBA0VqMi4sPN5LCKIJu4opLsQvt\niVvZUjQ7D26Pwrhl9dtNkEBAIToNmwKoTDWQjqJBp4RDPlqFzoqvH7tQMtgLl12X\ntJRak/WH5haRSHVUwSFie83Qz2YFS996Y3WG2HkIQzvhAtnvFeQNDc/9/E9tWueX\nlbKf1OthjiUartvibx+HyUU5STuVkYjNMmy+td7ZAzf3CtkA3y+wua/LOLppY5k+\na20eWHo4ZWZKl62Pc/dG\n=S90n\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 220d08690e900748bcb99ab3a7df68ff143f2cc4\nparent 9100f2c68203819ecd69ad71862b47336e8f725a\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1781816027 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781816027 -0400\n\nrelease(langgraph): 1.2.6 (#8139)","verified_at":"2026-06-18T20:53:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/ce6c8b2410f9921d379c8fe8ea8087d1934c07a9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/ce6c8b2410f9921d379c8fe8ea8087d1934c07a9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/ce6c8b2410f9921d379c8fe8ea8087d1934c07a9/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9100f2c68203819ecd69ad71862b47336e8f725a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/9100f2c68203819ecd69ad71862b47336e8f725a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/9100f2c68203819ecd69ad71862b47336e8f725a"}]},{"sha":"9100f2c68203819ecd69ad71862b47336e8f725a","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKDkxMDBmMmM2ODIwMzgxOWVjZDY5YWQ3MTg2MmI0NzMzNmU4ZjcyNWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Quanzheng Long","email":"long@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-17T17:50:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T17:50:30Z"},"message":"feat: add delta-channel-dump recovery script as examples to dump from Postgres for deltaChannel rollback (#8109)\n\nAdd a standalone recovery tool at `examples/delta-channel-dump/` for\noperators rolling back from langgraph >= 1.2 / deepagents 0.6.x to an\nolder runtime that does not understand `EXT_DELTA_SNAPSHOT` msgpack\nblobs. Without this, channels like `messages` can appear empty after\nrollback because the old reducer does not decode delta snapshots.\n\n`dump.py` connects directly to Postgres, walks the checkpoint parent\nchain (mirroring `aget_delta_channel_history`), decodes msgpack blobs\nvia `ormsgpack` with a hand-rolled EXT 0–7 hook (no langgraph imports),\nand emits JSON with per-channel `seed` + oldest-to-newest `writes`. The\noperator reduces and re-applies via `update_state` manually.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Postgres checkpointer only\n- Deps: `psycopg[binary]`, `ormsgpack` (not added to repo\n`pyproject.toml` — operator installs at runtime)\n- No reducer application, no DB writes, no AES/custom encryption support\n(fails loudly on encrypted blob types)\n\n## How verified\n\n- E2E against local Postgres: 15 runs of `delta_channel_messages_freq`\n(`snapshot_frequency=10`)\n- Asserted `delta_kind == \"snapshot\"`, `len(seed) == 10`, `len(writes)\n== 5`, message ids `ai-0`..`ai-14`\n- Confirmed portability: fresh venv with only `pip install\n\"psycopg[binary]\" ormsgpack` produced identical output","tree":{"sha":"b97ddfafb344c1b513e1300451a83c9a7c10f9e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/b97ddfafb344c1b513e1300451a83c9a7c10f9e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/9100f2c68203819ecd69ad71862b47336e8f725a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMt5mCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjLgQAEsesyfL2XER488PplF+FJF/\njZNIoMdArWTN8JWAzYXD1+t4Wftu0Lo7gCmqc11YnCItHieaF7NYQLfleKeNnqB1\neHrOCg36B5QMLpn+jLVu4oZiK2Z6y5jUWC9fgsiQNluge0qR3anuu8dT9GdcnnT8\nL6ydrtQVOf5ldQUeL0xdQMC02EIpHST0o4rNqrGo98qqpjMVUJ+gelJinNOATu0x\nw8TrWwC5Tl53pg0SUAtvw/6BIASfjYoJzI0hwfDhTvgkZDqxUjEEZifWjjVUE+9z\nh1csaSeyuFEvYnn7LFahAJ9lDk4Prc3TboWPUebC6+yP8O3+dg8ALsS1ufvLH0Px\nFDmCR0vXm8uE6UygdHXNcTALprJee5dPUTqnt9w2UodwX3jaYLElGZy2l2e0iQRy\n7Jllgz51+QSSbEmXsaGOkg8lkmwVpAR0llANE9hGkBScwkrGEvUfxTe/MkZXOl1M\nC+Eygj51sUa/EScT9TbcIJnGcwyEp7ogSTgtHYcWnyx/4HZKYevvVekuubz0OefO\nx7t9fGfBgO47SNDfZFN07Eya0MURgiQCdWLZR4SkijGISON3t+J+UAEQG6ZSSaDz\nzNKZEFHYVLdWQN1nhX4+aGMqW3JKo5u72lPYjfTGsYjAXAOZGhjaQQ3lZurwEcIk\nh0Bz6iQI5hJNPH3osUft\n=cQ78\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b97ddfafb344c1b513e1300451a83c9a7c10f9e1\nparent 79befe67ba2568ae2c90349b01e65d6f7a38765a\nauthor Quanzheng Long <long@langchain.dev> 1781718630 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781718630 -0700\n\nfeat: add delta-channel-dump recovery script as examples to dump from Postgres for deltaChannel rollback (#8109)\n\nAdd a standalone recovery tool at `examples/delta-channel-dump/` for\noperators rolling back from langgraph >= 1.2 / deepagents 0.6.x to an\nolder runtime that does not understand `EXT_DELTA_SNAPSHOT` msgpack\nblobs. Without this, channels like `messages` can appear empty after\nrollback because the old reducer does not decode delta snapshots.\n\n`dump.py` connects directly to Postgres, walks the checkpoint parent\nchain (mirroring `aget_delta_channel_history`), decodes msgpack blobs\nvia `ormsgpack` with a hand-rolled EXT 0–7 hook (no langgraph imports),\nand emits JSON with per-channel `seed` + oldest-to-newest `writes`. The\noperator reduces and re-applies via `update_state` manually.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Postgres checkpointer only\n- Deps: `psycopg[binary]`, `ormsgpack` (not added to repo\n`pyproject.toml` — operator installs at runtime)\n- No reducer application, no DB writes, no AES/custom encryption support\n(fails loudly on encrypted blob types)\n\n## How verified\n\n- E2E against local Postgres: 15 runs of `delta_channel_messages_freq`\n(`snapshot_frequency=10`)\n- Asserted `delta_kind == \"snapshot\"`, `len(seed) == 10`, `len(writes)\n== 5`, message ids `ai-0`..`ai-14`\n- Confirmed portability: fresh venv with only `pip install\n\"psycopg[binary]\" ormsgpack` produced identical output","verified_at":"2026-06-17T17:50:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/9100f2c68203819ecd69ad71862b47336e8f725a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/9100f2c68203819ecd69ad71862b47336e8f725a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/9100f2c68203819ecd69ad71862b47336e8f725a/comments","author":null,"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"79befe67ba2568ae2c90349b01e65d6f7a38765a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/79befe67ba2568ae2c90349b01e65d6f7a38765a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/79befe67ba2568ae2c90349b01e65d6f7a38765a"}]},{"sha":"79befe67ba2568ae2c90349b01e65d6f7a38765a","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKDc5YmVmZTY3YmEyNTY4YWUyYzkwMzQ5YjAxZTY1ZDZmN2EzODc2NWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-17T14:29:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T14:29:31Z"},"message":"fix: nested subgraph inherits parent checkpoint_ns (regression in 1.2.3) (#8053)\n\nCloses #8038\n\n## Description\n\nThe `ensure_config` merge introduced in #7926 caused a child graph\ninvoked inside a parent node to inherit the parent task's\n`checkpoint_ns` from the ambient run context\n(`var_child_runnable_config`), so the child's checkpoints were written\nunder an unreadable namespace and re-ran from scratch each turn (#8038).\nThe first explicitly passed `configurable` that carries a checkpoint\ncoordinate (a `thread_id`, or any\n`checkpoint_ns`/`checkpoint_id`/`checkpoint_map`) now replaces the\nambient one, while subsequent explicit configs still shallow-merge —\npreserving #7926's `with_config(...)` semantics.\n\n## Contract\n\n`ensure_config` merges an explicit `configurable` over the ambient run\ncontext (`var_child_runnable_config`) with one rule: **an explicit\n`configurable` that supplies its own checkpoint coordinate addresses its\nown checkpoint lineage, so the ambient `configurable` is dropped rather\nthan merged over.** Coordinate keys are `thread_id`, `checkpoint_ns`,\n`checkpoint_id`, and `checkpoint_map` (grouped as\n`_CHECKPOINT_COORDINATE_KEYS`). A non-coordinate `configurable` keeps\nthe ambient and shallow-merges over it.\n\nBelow, each case shows the parent/child graph wiring that triggers it\nand the resulting namespacing. The child is always a compiled subgraph\ninvoked from inside a parent node.\n\n### 1. Subgraph invoked with no new config → ambient inherited\n\n```python\nchild = StateGraph(ChildState).add_node(\"n\", child_node).add_edge(START, \"n\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\n\ndef parent_node(state):\n    child.invoke({}, config=None)          # no explicit configurable\n    return {\"result\": \"ok\"}\n\nparent = StateGraph(ParentState).add_node(\"p\", parent_node).add_edge(START, \"p\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\nparent.invoke({\"result\": \"\"}, config={\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": \"parent\"}})\n```\nChild inherits the parent task's `checkpoint_ns` (`p:<parent-task>`);\nits checkpoints are written as a discoverable child of the parent run.\nPre-#7926 behavior, unchanged.\n\n### 2. Subgraph invoked with a new thread_id → ambient dropped\n\n```python\nchild = StateGraph(ChildState).add_node(\"n\", child_node).add_edge(START, \"n\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\nchild_config = {\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": str(uuid4())}}\n\ndef parent_node(state):\n    child.invoke({}, config=child_config)  # explicit new thread_id\n    return {\"result\": \"ok\"}\n\nparent = StateGraph(ParentState).add_node(\"p\", parent_node).add_edge(START, \"p\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\nparent.invoke({\"result\": \"\"}, config={\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": \"parent\"}})\n```\nChild starts its own lineage on `child_config`'s thread; `checkpoint_ns\n== \"\"`; `child.get_state(child_config)` reads back state across repeated\nparent turns. Fixes #8038.\n\n### 3. Subgraph invoked with the same thread_id as parent → ambient\nstill dropped\n\n```python\nchild = StateGraph(ChildState).add_node(\"n\", child_node).add_edge(START, \"n\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\n\ndef parent_node(state):\n    # reuses the parent's thread_id as the child's own\n    child.invoke({}, config={\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": state[\"parent_thread\"]}})\n    return {\"result\": \"ok\"}\n\nparent = StateGraph(ParentState).add_node(\"p\", parent_node).add_edge(START, \"p\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\nparent_thread = str(uuid4())\nparent.invoke({\"parent_thread\": parent_thread, \"result\": \"\"}, config={\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": parent_thread}})\n```\nChild addresses its own root namespace on the shared thread;\n`checkpoint_ns == \"\"`. The parent task's `checkpoint_ns` must not leak\nin, or `child.get_state({\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": parent_thread}})`\nreturns empty state and the child re-runs from scratch each turn.\n\n### 4. Subagent invoked with a non-coordinate key only → ambient\ninherited\n\n```python\nchild = StateGraph(ChildState).add_node(\"n\", child_node).add_edge(START, \"n\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\n\ndef parent_node(state):\n    # ls_agent_type is not a checkpoint coordinate, so ambient is kept\n    child.invoke({}, config={\"configurable\": {\"ls_agent_type\": \"subagent\"}})\n    return {\"result\": \"ok\"}\n\nparent = StateGraph(ParentState).add_node(\"p\", parent_node).add_edge(START, \"p\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\nparent.invoke({\"result\": \"\"}, config={\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": \"parent\"}})\n```\nChild remains a discoverable child of the parent run; ambient\n`thread_id` and `checkpoint_ns` preserved (deepagents `task` tool\npattern).\n\n### 5. with_config(...) + invoke-time thread_id → ambient dropped, then\nmerged\n\n```python\n# child compiled with a non-coordinate configurable via with_config\nchild = (\n    StateGraph(ChildState)\n    .add_node(\"n\", child_node)\n    .add_edge(START, \"n\")\n    .compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\n    .with_config({\"configurable\": {\"ls_agent_type\": \"root\"}})\n)\n\ndef parent_node(state):\n    # invoke-time config supplies the thread_id; with_config's ls_agent_type survives\n    child.invoke({}, config={\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": \"child\"}})\n    return {\"result\": \"ok\"}\n\nparent = StateGraph(ParentState).add_node(\"p\", parent_node).add_edge(START, \"p\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\nparent.invoke({\"result\": \"\"}, config={\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": \"parent\"}})\n```\nFirst coordinate-bearing config (`thread_id`) drops the ambient;\nsubsequent explicit configs still shallow-merge, so `ls_agent_type`\nsurvives alongside `thread_id`. Preserves #7926 `with_config(...)`\nsemantics.\n\n### Regression note\n\nCases 1, 4, and 5 are the pre-#7926 behavior and are preserved\nunchanged. Cases 2 and 3 fix the regression introduced by #7926: an\nexplicit `thread_id` resets the ambient even when it equals the ambient\nthread id, because a child reusing the parent's thread id still\naddresses its own root namespace on that thread, not the parent task's.\n\n## Self-Hosted Release Note\nFix regression where a nested subgraph with its own `thread_id` invoked\ninside a parent node lost its persisted state across turns.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_subgraph_persistence.py -k\ntest_child_with_own_thread_id_keeps_namespace` (case 2)\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_utils.py -k\nensure_config_explicit_configurable_replaces_ambient` (case 2)\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_utils.py -k\nensure_config_ambient_inherited_when_no_explicit_configurable` (case 1)\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_utils.py -k\nensure_config_non_coordinate_config_keeps_ambient_checkpoint_ns` (case\n4)\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_utils.py -k\nensure_config_explicit_configurables_still_merge_over_ambient` (case 5)\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_utils.py -k\nensure_config_same_thread_id_still_clears_ambient` (case 3)\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Hollon <274035459+nick-hollon-lc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"92c776071306c0e7ad1eb3274687593ff195ff14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/92c776071306c0e7ad1eb3274687593ff195ff14"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/79befe67ba2568ae2c90349b01e65d6f7a38765a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMq9LCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOlIQAHVsa7LicjvVLVpblVkr7GB/\nNezYMdwYevUglPT/TMn4r2cMCfr1zrsQu+9YVloQda2JgXCH/cgmUVP00wvYFLmw\nfEBOGisKit74aHk+BlG5NeceiluIKPoPReW+hW0DW0may27g7nU8tJa9KjNGwq/d\nxvaKL7I2K4bKP3B1By59M31UPiTxVtCD8Z9OhGH84DUtuLB49hZ+ngXQ85kno9w4\nJYnUhINhk7jfhSCs69infaDExEpYUuhLhnrkIJPys5Vv9UoiGSGP9QFhJULMtWod\n4i+8timl1xQsS/P6B5mi3dxJmi+IR/EjnRhxWe6yU+ftlu7+gtMZ1FxW5jdJ8a4X\n2wHYlEnJLCoz0TBZDHiqSK79Xcevkitekve0qsRliwOraZV4oez0/tS0ENUIY1t1\nceCBSPtr5vciFNYoRVOytQruKSSPlIibE068IRdUQd9DXu9zRXme9UIgldbtN1Ee\nbV2CoAGkACk1nWSkxcg3TSK4z+Ya58zLUj/ofIFCzprjzpxpMVOcwCk87ippJMzh\ntsR7GIeEV3n80EgNDWiyjiWKkqsDCpFfO2+vSWLWT1wMV51iEwfhMq4aPMVG5cTB\nzxlC13pyJ/Si+Cqfz4Jy4WD4ST3XOOpTzT/k6OHZ5R9/J8d7qocuhfj068kgDnMw\nGAFfFoiyDjzn1o8PUkug\n=7Zao\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 92c776071306c0e7ad1eb3274687593ff195ff14\nparent 9af25217c36ad031e6b1231a6bccdfdb0dc70a16\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1781706571 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781706571 -0400\n\nfix: nested subgraph inherits parent checkpoint_ns (regression in 1.2.3) (#8053)\n\nCloses #8038\n\n## Description\n\nThe `ensure_config` merge introduced in #7926 caused a child graph\ninvoked inside a parent node to inherit the parent task's\n`checkpoint_ns` from the ambient run context\n(`var_child_runnable_config`), so the child's checkpoints were written\nunder an unreadable namespace and re-ran from scratch each turn (#8038).\nThe first explicitly passed `configurable` that carries a checkpoint\ncoordinate (a `thread_id`, or any\n`checkpoint_ns`/`checkpoint_id`/`checkpoint_map`) now replaces the\nambient one, while subsequent explicit configs still shallow-merge —\npreserving #7926's `with_config(...)` semantics.\n\n## Contract\n\n`ensure_config` merges an explicit `configurable` over the ambient run\ncontext (`var_child_runnable_config`) with one rule: **an explicit\n`configurable` that supplies its own checkpoint coordinate addresses its\nown checkpoint lineage, so the ambient `configurable` is dropped rather\nthan merged over.** Coordinate keys are `thread_id`, `checkpoint_ns`,\n`checkpoint_id`, and `checkpoint_map` (grouped as\n`_CHECKPOINT_COORDINATE_KEYS`). A non-coordinate `configurable` keeps\nthe ambient and shallow-merges over it.\n\nBelow, each case shows the parent/child graph wiring that triggers it\nand the resulting namespacing. The child is always a compiled subgraph\ninvoked from inside a parent node.\n\n### 1. Subgraph invoked with no new config → ambient inherited\n\n```python\nchild = StateGraph(ChildState).add_node(\"n\", child_node).add_edge(START, \"n\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\n\ndef parent_node(state):\n    child.invoke({}, config=None)          # no explicit configurable\n    return {\"result\": \"ok\"}\n\nparent = StateGraph(ParentState).add_node(\"p\", parent_node).add_edge(START, \"p\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\nparent.invoke({\"result\": \"\"}, config={\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": \"parent\"}})\n```\nChild inherits the parent task's `checkpoint_ns` (`p:<parent-task>`);\nits checkpoints are written as a discoverable child of the parent run.\nPre-#7926 behavior, unchanged.\n\n### 2. Subgraph invoked with a new thread_id → ambient dropped\n\n```python\nchild = StateGraph(ChildState).add_node(\"n\", child_node).add_edge(START, \"n\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\nchild_config = {\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": str(uuid4())}}\n\ndef parent_node(state):\n    child.invoke({}, config=child_config)  # explicit new thread_id\n    return {\"result\": \"ok\"}\n\nparent = StateGraph(ParentState).add_node(\"p\", parent_node).add_edge(START, \"p\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\nparent.invoke({\"result\": \"\"}, config={\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": \"parent\"}})\n```\nChild starts its own lineage on `child_config`'s thread; `checkpoint_ns\n== \"\"`; `child.get_state(child_config)` reads back state across repeated\nparent turns. Fixes #8038.\n\n### 3. Subgraph invoked with the same thread_id as parent → ambient\nstill dropped\n\n```python\nchild = StateGraph(ChildState).add_node(\"n\", child_node).add_edge(START, \"n\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\n\ndef parent_node(state):\n    # reuses the parent's thread_id as the child's own\n    child.invoke({}, config={\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": state[\"parent_thread\"]}})\n    return {\"result\": \"ok\"}\n\nparent = StateGraph(ParentState).add_node(\"p\", parent_node).add_edge(START, \"p\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\nparent_thread = str(uuid4())\nparent.invoke({\"parent_thread\": parent_thread, \"result\": \"\"}, config={\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": parent_thread}})\n```\nChild addresses its own root namespace on the shared thread;\n`checkpoint_ns == \"\"`. The parent task's `checkpoint_ns` must not leak\nin, or `child.get_state({\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": parent_thread}})`\nreturns empty state and the child re-runs from scratch each turn.\n\n### 4. Subagent invoked with a non-coordinate key only → ambient\ninherited\n\n```python\nchild = StateGraph(ChildState).add_node(\"n\", child_node).add_edge(START, \"n\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\n\ndef parent_node(state):\n    # ls_agent_type is not a checkpoint coordinate, so ambient is kept\n    child.invoke({}, config={\"configurable\": {\"ls_agent_type\": \"subagent\"}})\n    return {\"result\": \"ok\"}\n\nparent = StateGraph(ParentState).add_node(\"p\", parent_node).add_edge(START, \"p\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\nparent.invoke({\"result\": \"\"}, config={\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": \"parent\"}})\n```\nChild remains a discoverable child of the parent run; ambient\n`thread_id` and `checkpoint_ns` preserved (deepagents `task` tool\npattern).\n\n### 5. with_config(...) + invoke-time thread_id → ambient dropped, then\nmerged\n\n```python\n# child compiled with a non-coordinate configurable via with_config\nchild = (\n    StateGraph(ChildState)\n    .add_node(\"n\", child_node)\n    .add_edge(START, \"n\")\n    .compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\n    .with_config({\"configurable\": {\"ls_agent_type\": \"root\"}})\n)\n\ndef parent_node(state):\n    # invoke-time config supplies the thread_id; with_config's ls_agent_type survives\n    child.invoke({}, config={\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": \"child\"}})\n    return {\"result\": \"ok\"}\n\nparent = StateGraph(ParentState).add_node(\"p\", parent_node).add_edge(START, \"p\").compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\nparent.invoke({\"result\": \"\"}, config={\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": \"parent\"}})\n```\nFirst coordinate-bearing config (`thread_id`) drops the ambient;\nsubsequent explicit configs still shallow-merge, so `ls_agent_type`\nsurvives alongside `thread_id`. Preserves #7926 `with_config(...)`\nsemantics.\n\n### Regression note\n\nCases 1, 4, and 5 are the pre-#7926 behavior and are preserved\nunchanged. Cases 2 and 3 fix the regression introduced by #7926: an\nexplicit `thread_id` resets the ambient even when it equals the ambient\nthread id, because a child reusing the parent's thread id still\naddresses its own root namespace on that thread, not the parent task's.\n\n## Self-Hosted Release Note\nFix regression where a nested subgraph with its own `thread_id` invoked\ninside a parent node lost its persisted state across turns.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_subgraph_persistence.py -k\ntest_child_with_own_thread_id_keeps_namespace` (case 2)\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_utils.py -k\nensure_config_explicit_configurable_replaces_ambient` (case 2)\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_utils.py -k\nensure_config_ambient_inherited_when_no_explicit_configurable` (case 1)\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_utils.py -k\nensure_config_non_coordinate_config_keeps_ambient_checkpoint_ns` (case\n4)\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_utils.py -k\nensure_config_explicit_configurables_still_merge_over_ambient` (case 5)\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_utils.py -k\nensure_config_same_thread_id_still_clears_ambient` (case 3)\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Hollon <274035459+nick-hollon-lc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T14:29:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/79befe67ba2568ae2c90349b01e65d6f7a38765a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/79befe67ba2568ae2c90349b01e65d6f7a38765a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/79befe67ba2568ae2c90349b01e65d6f7a38765a/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9af25217c36ad031e6b1231a6bccdfdb0dc70a16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/9af25217c36ad031e6b1231a6bccdfdb0dc70a16","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/9af25217c36ad031e6b1231a6bccdfdb0dc70a16"}]},{"sha":"9af25217c36ad031e6b1231a6bccdfdb0dc70a16","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKDlhZjI1MjE3YzM2YWQwMzFlNmIxMjMxYTZiY2NkZmRiMGRjNzBhMTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-17T13:40:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T13:40:05Z"},"message":"fix: cancel running subgraphs on v3 stream abort [closes #8029] (#8057)\n\n## Description\nv3 event streaming's `stream.abort()` (sync and async) only closed the\nmux and stopped pumping, leaving the underlying `astream`/`stream`\ngenerator — and any running subgraphs — alive until they finished,\nburning resources. The fix closes the underlying graph iterator so\n`GeneratorExit` propagates into in-flight nodes/subgraphs and cancels\nthem, matching v2's `aclose()` behavior. Fixes #8029.\n\n## Release Note\nv3 streaming `stream.abort()` now cancels running subgraphs instead of\nletting them run to completion.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `TEST=\"tests/test_pregel_stream_events_v3.py -k abort\" make test`\n(new `test_abort_cancels_running_subgraph` asserts the looping subgraph\nstops after abort)\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Hollon <274035459+nick-hollon-lc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"23d43b33030d1175a0bf1b0c49f01517b2891e06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/23d43b33030d1175a0bf1b0c49f01517b2891e06"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/9af25217c36ad031e6b1231a6bccdfdb0dc70a16","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMqO1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYKsQAGGmamh6WydM/c3dEIRRWoJB\nqcN+2Mal0FEJazKhdsMKnnu99pfRy1AQucZI56n6VONwNAgJQFgA4hp8edJp2WVv\nbHLX+ng1s5tpsvxQ+bTpYNBH6cZAhCzcrXWyBu0ylzUQeHxljBCxNuQUnHttho8f\nG17xYNokmtynTnidNDpTdl6sKupCYNokD2dJbhVasycu7GwZxmo/DiAAv/+i9CEX\nLsh3yKma7OSdKFLT3MVkY4ymVCcVtPZWlmf1J7O7R2+thp/zIjSscr3uMHHGlb3t\neX5OmxtPhLJt14+6kz+xCKW3Ug+LnZBI4/gUK+qIJ/dUYv2IfrUysXtU4hXaV67v\n6lOC75G95KCVoQiqpPokoHmVchiaGCCpzcTRNX/LMYpDDevmZQNKvREbNyrl8wLN\nP2iIdFxsknvy6+9l1MA3VMN0oF95KSR2ugt9lX+Az2lSj4LiumZyV1PfZhnAQlyy\nMQxP64MTSnh20OAdyE8nwslI0nEqle/rLlPNrKYY5eWin9xlMdImRnOiQgv1yPRI\nwATToPac/WUEDPUvyCWJiMqMKX+Vnqy85bWUN8rIluEPuPZEFk2lOontiLmXWYVw\nliyYXuP55C/skUKgRNEEVklO29x4im4zhMtsNT05O9b88Ph5I2gTOSWXUxIYvF7s\ncgDnbSzgHT8vRcSEh/qi\n=bM4o\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 23d43b33030d1175a0bf1b0c49f01517b2891e06\nparent 1a9baae9592e0c21336f6e09c891ba75481fd657\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1781703605 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781703605 -0400\n\nfix: cancel running subgraphs on v3 stream abort [closes #8029] (#8057)\n\n## Description\nv3 event streaming's `stream.abort()` (sync and async) only closed the\nmux and stopped pumping, leaving the underlying `astream`/`stream`\ngenerator — and any running subgraphs — alive until they finished,\nburning resources. The fix closes the underlying graph iterator so\n`GeneratorExit` propagates into in-flight nodes/subgraphs and cancels\nthem, matching v2's `aclose()` behavior. Fixes #8029.\n\n## Release Note\nv3 streaming `stream.abort()` now cancels running subgraphs instead of\nletting them run to completion.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `TEST=\"tests/test_pregel_stream_events_v3.py -k abort\" make test`\n(new `test_abort_cancels_running_subgraph` asserts the looping subgraph\nstops after abort)\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Hollon <274035459+nick-hollon-lc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T13:40:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/9af25217c36ad031e6b1231a6bccdfdb0dc70a16","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/9af25217c36ad031e6b1231a6bccdfdb0dc70a16","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/9af25217c36ad031e6b1231a6bccdfdb0dc70a16/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1a9baae9592e0c21336f6e09c891ba75481fd657","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/1a9baae9592e0c21336f6e09c891ba75481fd657","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/1a9baae9592e0c21336f6e09c891ba75481fd657"}]},{"sha":"1a9baae9592e0c21336f6e09c891ba75481fd657","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKDFhOWJhYWU5NTkyZTBjMjEzMzZmNmUwOWM4OTFiYTc1NDgxZmQ2NTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Connor Braa","email":"3478454+cwlbraa@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-16T19:43:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T19:43:04Z"},"message":"release(cli): 0.4.30 (#8101)\n\nBump langgraph-cli to 0.4.30 to cut a CLI release from\n916025d2f6d9f6ddb2628bd248bc4f3db632d9a8.\n\nAlso change the in-memory extra to require langgraph-api <0.12.0,\nexcluding 0.12.0.dev releases from normal pip resolution.\n\nRefresh uv example lockfiles so they keep langchain-protocol compatible\nwith the stable API image used by CLI integration tests.\n\nCI will verify the release change.","tree":{"sha":"8a98a70277924b1f366dba2aa8b570da3ec3a176","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/8a98a70277924b1f366dba2aa8b570da3ec3a176"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/1a9baae9592e0c21336f6e09c891ba75481fd657","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMadICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxRYQAGV8IyBzTt4DEc2OCwqw9GdU\nm21K62pKjHzLp04nrIv0sMX3KuzdM8bOpm9ir0V6Y8iN2j6tJmhWTJ6iuoZLlbN6\nVJ728cgyWH+Kamd0JahbQqoJ0XL0sDYTY2XAXEZQSpnKujb8Djb3sEpAjTWq7T8t\nJKMbyj8mVG4uKIsbmYhYHzePCAInjZWlAlF7sgcSkdnOq043cE2jO4zUFVgcNXRP\nFS4Mwju3bxCyEYyP91RXDCTqCRHACdf7absO1surUXo4EdQq/QXDhifYG553y3Po\nzkZ4v/reIfyevdi94IrWj7ETHfJLdcwxDydJS7H3N7yez11tcAcaILeALl84Rxvd\nKJOZ5K241PI/fuJHDFt1VW11BjCu8e0OzonejeUWD93n6QSUpaJ4GLctjw5XptM2\nHgNdCx/Uho54BFDoepKhbnbJFnfNvu8cVN1zVMNoXHtF2gGGATYnWr3VQo2Akc28\nNzCl29Z5Yhz28r97rBdIOksfx+99yt8639un1Nd+O4P3dyT7HEjHXGn6u10qg+y7\nbqDzgTkNiNZvOrCXE0RF1XtUZY3BrOnXuzKjDKDXFUZWAfBG7JfDS1QBbWQsQDhn\nYWIyoTlOhtyjJbQ34KJD5wkohvRlD6IKqvXrj9T3Tb8JE7Pv4eXI9wxSRe7oO3Zq\ntRI5L854WwZ/fktoboWB\n=Y7Th\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8a98a70277924b1f366dba2aa8b570da3ec3a176\nparent 916025d2f6d9f6ddb2628bd248bc4f3db632d9a8\nauthor Connor Braa <3478454+cwlbraa@users.noreply.github.com> 1781638984 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781638984 -0700\n\nrelease(cli): 0.4.30 (#8101)\n\nBump langgraph-cli to 0.4.30 to cut a CLI release from\n916025d2f6d9f6ddb2628bd248bc4f3db632d9a8.\n\nAlso change the in-memory extra to require langgraph-api <0.12.0,\nexcluding 0.12.0.dev releases from normal pip resolution.\n\nRefresh uv example lockfiles so they keep langchain-protocol compatible\nwith the stable API image used by CLI integration tests.\n\nCI will verify the release change.","verified_at":"2026-06-16T19:43:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/1a9baae9592e0c21336f6e09c891ba75481fd657","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/1a9baae9592e0c21336f6e09c891ba75481fd657","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/1a9baae9592e0c21336f6e09c891ba75481fd657/comments","author":{"login":"cwlbraa","id":3478454,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0Nzg0NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3478454?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa","html_url":"https://github.com/cwlbraa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"916025d2f6d9f6ddb2628bd248bc4f3db632d9a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/916025d2f6d9f6ddb2628bd248bc4f3db632d9a8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/916025d2f6d9f6ddb2628bd248bc4f3db632d9a8"}]},{"sha":"916025d2f6d9f6ddb2628bd248bc4f3db632d9a8","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKDkxNjAyNWQyZjZkOWY2ZGRiMjYyOGJkMjQ4YmM0ZjNkYjYzMmQ5YTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Connor Braa","email":"3478454+cwlbraa@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-16T00:24:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T00:24:31Z"},"message":"feat(cli): support compatible api version ranges (#8023)\n\nAdds `api_version` ranges for LangGraph API base image tags.\n`~=0.11.0.dev5` resolves to the newest matching compatible image while\nfreezing later dev prereleases until rc/final/patch tags exist;\n`>~=0.11.0.dev5` uses the same floor but can also float to future stable\nreleases while ignoring future prereleases.\n\nVerified with `make format`, `make lint`, and `make test` from\n`libs/cli`.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Connor Braa <cwlbraa@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"547ca13ba2fb9107007f9c9ce984f6ab22e10f35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/547ca13ba2fb9107007f9c9ce984f6ab22e10f35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/916025d2f6d9f6ddb2628bd248bc4f3db632d9a8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMJe/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJCAQAJH/QPBi2GHxkY3ax+ue+R1Y\nJmTWQB2DCdyhCEOLzx6cnVQ1UGqOx3Dzuo5zT2cjPwmHCgDMRV99gJa2Q8WhuKC7\n/9oAk2lyc7PXNnMSDgeR+wQboueGUD+1wTI/EgNKZwjtE6p1nXHr4n4AKrMvA8Sr\njoJchqRFiNSYAUtc0a1Iu46kRSQE2WEGVT2AvgGG8Mfr1REelDQ6lrNaDXf0iDcb\n5xva7FK2Xi3Wf72hOvZJJB/hYhMOgCZRW4Ck0hTTZD4K12SDpO7k3H0NupI8YtAV\nuzbv17+FzeshLKjOEvhmMi2O4d6KVYkpy3nmm4HQZEOk/5XW6/Yl5B+we3a+/Yx5\nQdb90oKC9HxB84CgND3gvXy0kM4AXVY0GytDyMBrKXlf5g86+mauQmUU4xvOhJVY\nT8LwnaVWS3zB2gW4atMSRfwdMQzCXNud1vPcG2k+nZKSKrJx2mFYuHN+zkhdEQxy\n1b7MSOv9YwHTt8wbssaj75C9dCf8osZ9FXU7sXc9QBYdzxlvLbuJDrNOdNSFNkk8\nETn+UP9LOuIm7VrsTbbKhjAwfKhPhtMez5TeBnsiUwFBQPQEMj3DRStdqyIqp/9Q\nLPbsVLjJo9XQeUbDZwGgV5UuHN5MKPgSqBL5z8hkwcrG5NAIbOldb2x0PnywIbaZ\nCJ3FsWVFYE+6WbBj0PAM\n=z3pR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 547ca13ba2fb9107007f9c9ce984f6ab22e10f35\nparent 97320843fe78b93bd5290ce366841ff9850bf379\nauthor Connor Braa <3478454+cwlbraa@users.noreply.github.com> 1781569471 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781569471 -0400\n\nfeat(cli): support compatible api version ranges (#8023)\n\nAdds `api_version` ranges for LangGraph API base image tags.\n`~=0.11.0.dev5` resolves to the newest matching compatible image while\nfreezing later dev prereleases until rc/final/patch tags exist;\n`>~=0.11.0.dev5` uses the same floor but can also float to future stable\nreleases while ignoring future prereleases.\n\nVerified with `make format`, `make lint`, and `make test` from\n`libs/cli`.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Connor Braa <cwlbraa@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-06-16T00:24:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/916025d2f6d9f6ddb2628bd248bc4f3db632d9a8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/916025d2f6d9f6ddb2628bd248bc4f3db632d9a8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/916025d2f6d9f6ddb2628bd248bc4f3db632d9a8/comments","author":{"login":"cwlbraa","id":3478454,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0Nzg0NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3478454?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa","html_url":"https://github.com/cwlbraa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwlbraa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"97320843fe78b93bd5290ce366841ff9850bf379","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/97320843fe78b93bd5290ce366841ff9850bf379","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/97320843fe78b93bd5290ce366841ff9850bf379"}]},{"sha":"97320843fe78b93bd5290ce366841ff9850bf379","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKDk3MzIwODQzZmU3OGI5M2JkNTI5MGNlMzY2ODQxZmY5ODUwYmYzNzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-13T01:29:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-13T01:29:40Z"},"message":"ci(deps): pin GitHub Actions to commit SHAs (#8065)\n\nEvery third-party GitHub Action in the workflows is now pinned to a full\ncommit SHA instead of a floating major tag, closing a supply-chain gap\nwhere a mutable tag like `@v6` could be force-pushed to point at\nmalicious code. Seven actions were already SHA-pinned; this brings the\nremaining first-party `actions/*` and `astral-sh/setup-uv` references in\nline.\n\n## Changes\n- Pinned all previously tag-referenced actions to their current commit\nSHA with the exact release as a trailing comment (the format Dependabot\nreads and updates): `actions/checkout` → `v6.0.3`,\n`actions/setup-python` → `v6.2.0`, `actions/github-script` → `v9.0.0`,\n`actions/upload-artifact` → `v7.0.1`, `actions/download-artifact` →\n`v8.0.1`, `actions/cache/{restore,save}` → `v5.0.5`,\n`actions/configure-pages` → `v6.0.0`, `actions/deploy-pages` → `v5.0.0`,\n`actions/upload-pages-artifact` → `v5.0.0`,\n`actions/create-github-app-token` → `v3.2.0`, and `astral-sh/setup-uv` →\n`v7.6.0`.\n- Applied across all workflow files plus the `uv_setup` composite\naction; local same-repo references (`./.github/workflows/_*.yml`,\n`./.github/actions/uv_setup`) left as path refs since they resolve from\nthe same commit.","tree":{"sha":"79d58bed17f011ba41e6c5a3b367211afcb530fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/79d58bed17f011ba41e6c5a3b367211afcb530fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/97320843fe78b93bd5290ce366841ff9850bf379","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLLKECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALu0QAJZQOyKaF+hPkMWZXAqdiCMY\nrg7yE7BgHCeTScf8wqaWOmNEQjrVcbGS8jaQ+YFax/2JJnlv8nxF+DI/I1m5F81j\nLrGn1wVb9MHw+s0x6wecLougFu3/A1ZU8qtcrdrX8ugK7MdnEp44dnxCPBH5Szyp\n4ljImNiUAPyzlHQGFfFZt537uBItFnIwgNdZeCBKVTUaedag2725f/FyaK+CdpAY\nBmJVLVvzBbIhrToAQDoCdGpQsUkty/NFszUHgWXmIeFawrGTBXSFtSBr0VeQnHA1\nYFMaFPn6/GJCW2FGKr9cIMmfmSGL/Wl7/IZSmtxMG1uJ553dzoljxYcQlIgrRmXf\ndnVq2CXBtd7xgo4mYC+XU3+J9xQCE7rwxpkU/s37E7TWoyiciDZo5ADBZtl99+Zs\nkIkaL+vk0J6dYOnhdTLlCaPnuPVxmXCVabMsbD8W15Rr7Q19L1ucMUcbgfJe4ClU\nGw3Sg7I9zUc674zKHXz/B/k2sVCCueYHjv49FLy/thKgOH/P9iNcWyMDLvQ5g9Ls\n3T0dl7ZgHC8e0QLawTptS1cFS1UOiDhDWwsP1XoFaSKQ7oce4JnIw+EUFk7dZdn1\n0rnf2BdZ0DOjTk6RozenpC2Myv7YGRwfq4HEHIcxJQuqABwB9nU9KHyNVTmIriRG\ntioYPE5k6Q73EgihgALI\n=w5LI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 79d58bed17f011ba41e6c5a3b367211afcb530fd\nparent 8558481859c7951776954401841ce18609cdd1cc\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781314180 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781314180 -0400\n\nci(deps): pin GitHub Actions to commit SHAs (#8065)\n\nEvery third-party GitHub Action in the workflows is now pinned to a full\ncommit SHA instead of a floating major tag, closing a supply-chain gap\nwhere a mutable tag like `@v6` could be force-pushed to point at\nmalicious code. Seven actions were already SHA-pinned; this brings the\nremaining first-party `actions/*` and `astral-sh/setup-uv` references in\nline.\n\n## Changes\n- Pinned all previously tag-referenced actions to their current commit\nSHA with the exact release as a trailing comment (the format Dependabot\nreads and updates): `actions/checkout` → `v6.0.3`,\n`actions/setup-python` → `v6.2.0`, `actions/github-script` → `v9.0.0`,\n`actions/upload-artifact` → `v7.0.1`, `actions/download-artifact` →\n`v8.0.1`, `actions/cache/{restore,save}` → `v5.0.5`,\n`actions/configure-pages` → `v6.0.0`, `actions/deploy-pages` → `v5.0.0`,\n`actions/upload-pages-artifact` → `v5.0.0`,\n`actions/create-github-app-token` → `v3.2.0`, and `astral-sh/setup-uv` →\n`v7.6.0`.\n- Applied across all workflow files plus the `uv_setup` composite\naction; local same-repo references (`./.github/workflows/_*.yml`,\n`./.github/actions/uv_setup`) left as path refs since they resolve from\nthe same commit.","verified_at":"2026-06-13T01:29:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/97320843fe78b93bd5290ce366841ff9850bf379","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/97320843fe78b93bd5290ce366841ff9850bf379","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/97320843fe78b93bd5290ce366841ff9850bf379/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8558481859c7951776954401841ce18609cdd1cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/8558481859c7951776954401841ce18609cdd1cc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/8558481859c7951776954401841ce18609cdd1cc"}]}]